nsider whether `PlanDryRun` should print method+instance as \"完整单文件内容\". The task says \"--dry-run 输出完整单文件内容\". If the \"单文件\" is method+instance combined, then dry-run should print both.\n\nLet me reconsider the whole architecture. The \"单文件内聚\" means: instead of \"主 prompt 文件 + 多个 skill 文件散落（按路径引用）\", we want \"单文件内聚\" — skill/loop content inlined into a single .md product.\n\nFor plan, currently:\n- `plan_prompt.md` (instance) references `skill_grilling.md`, `skill_tdd_zh.md`, `skill_testing_anti_patterns_zh.md` by path (the `grilling_skill_path`, `tdd_skill_path`, `testing_anti_patterns_path` variables).\n- These skill files are written separately (scattered files).\n\nThe change: inline the grilling skill content into plan_prompt.md so pi doesn't need to load the scattered skill file.\n\nBut the KR1 note says \"method（system prompt）这一份自包含\". So actually the \"关键 loop/skill 内容\" (key loop/skill content) goes into method, while \"执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd）\" still use pi skills mechanism.\n\nWait, but then why does the boundary test check grilling content in `plan --dry-run` output?\n\nLet me re-examine: is grilling a \"关键 skill\" that gets inlined, or an \"执行期按需技能\" that stays as pi skills?\n\nThe KR1 note explicitly lists \"grilling/tdd 等\" as \"执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制\". So grilling should STAY as a pi skill (path), NOT be inlined into method.\n\nBut the boundary test requires grilling content inline in plan --dry-run output!\n\nThis is a contradiction between the KR note and the test. Let me re-read the KR note even more carefully:\n\n\"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\"\n\nHmm. So:\n- method (system prompt) is self-contained: key loop/skill content inlined into method.\n- On-demand skills (grilling/tdd) still use pi skills mechanism.\n\nSo the \"关键 loop/skill\" that gets inlined into method are the LOOPS (doing_loop, etc.) and the core skills that are part of the method, NOT grilling/tdd (which are on-demand execution skills).\n\nBut then what does the boundary test check? It checks grilling content inline in plan --dry-run.\n\nWait — maybe the distinction is: the method is self-contained (loops/skills inlined into method), AND the instance (user prompt) also inlines grilling content (so that pi doesn't need the scattered skill file for the plan command's grilling step).\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Let me look at the actual test more carefully and also the task10 plan's \"测试方法\" section 2 which is what task10.py is derived from:\n\nFrom task10.md 测试方法:\n\"2. 边界（单文件内聚）：前置条件 = build 成功；输入 = `plan --dry-run`；操作 = `./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep -cE 'Grilling|结构化追问'`；预期 = ≥1（grilling skill 内容内联进主产物，而非仅 `skill_grilling.md` 路径引用）。\"\n\nSo the test definitively requires grilling content inline in `plan --dry-run` output.\n\nSo regardless of the KR1 note's nuance, I need to make grilling content appear inline in the plan instance output (which is what plan --dry-run prints).\n\nNow, how to reconcile with \"method 自包含\"? I think the answer is:\n- Both method AND instance get the relevant inlining.\n- The method (system prompt) inlines the key loop content (e.g., the command's SOP already has it, and doing_loop content).\n- The instance (user prompt) inlines the on-demand skill content that the command's SOP references (grilling for plan, grilling for easy, etc.).\n\nActually, wait. Let me step back and think about what \"主产物\" means and what's simplest and most correct.\n\nThe simplest interpretation that satisfies all tests:\n1. `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)` in prompt package.\n2. `BuildPlan` reads grilling skill content and inlines it into the instance, replacing the `grilling_skill_path` variable (or setting a new variable like `grilling_content`).\n3. When grilling.md is missing, `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` returns error, and `BuildPlan` propagates it.\n\nBut wait, there's a subtlety. The plan.md template has:\n```\n4. **grilling 追问**：加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`），...\n```\n\nAnd also the `grilling_skill_path` variable is referenced. If I inline grilling content, I need to decide where. The template currently says \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\". \n\nI think the cleanest approach is:\n- Add a new variable to plan.md template like `{{grilling_content}}` that contains the full grilling skill content inline, and change the template to embed it. But wait, the task says \"本 task 只做结构内聚（产出形态），不改模板触发语言内容（task11）\". So I should NOT change the template's trigger language content. Hmm.\n\nActually \"不改模板触发语言内容\" means don't change the template's trigger language (task11 does that). But adding an inlining section is \"结构内聚（产出形态）\" which IS this task's job.\n\nWait, but KR3 says \"单文件含 pi 可识别的结构化引用（agent frontmatter / skill 内联段）\". So the single file should contain \"skill 内联段\" (skill inline sections).\n\nLet me look at how the template currently uses these variables, and design the inlining.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Maybe the cleanest approach that's consistent:\n\nThe plan.md template references `grilling_skill_path`, `tdd_skill_path`, `testing_anti_patterns_path`. These are \"scattered file paths\". The task wants to inline the CONTENT of these skills into the single .md product.\n\nSo I should:\n1. Read grilling skill content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")`.\n2. Read tdd skill content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"tdd-zh\")`.\n3. Read testing-anti-patterns content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"testing-anti-patterns-zh\")`.\n4. Inline these into the instance (plan_prompt.md).\n\nBut wait — the test only checks grilling. And the \"执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制\" suggests these should stay as pi skills. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider once more. Let me look at what \"关键 skill/loop\" means vs \"执行期按需技能\".\n\nLooking at the builder code, there are:\n- `doing_loop` — this is a loop (关键 loop), currently rendered via `renderDoingLoop` (LoadCoreSkills(\"doing_loop\")) and inlined into the doing instance as `doing_loop_content`. So doing_loop is ALREADY inlined.\n- `grilling`, `tdd-zh`, `testing-anti-patterns-zh`, `debug_skill`, `gen-skill`, `gen-loop`, `gen-domain`, `learning_loop`, `import_ctx` — these are skills that get written to files and referenced by path.\n\nWait, so `doing_loop` is already inlined (via LoadCoreSkills). But it uses `LoadCoreSkills` which is already an exported function in prompt package! And it logs a warning if missing but returns empty (no error).\n\nThe task wants:\n1. `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)` that wraps `skillsFS.ReadFile` and returns error when missing.\n2. The builder should use `ReadEmbeddedSkill` (not `LoadCoreSkills`) for the inlining.\n3. Key loop/skill content inlined into method (system prompt).\n\nHmm, but currently `doing_loop` is inlined into the instance (doing_loop_content variable in doing.md), not into method.\n\nLet me step back and think about the actual goal and what changes are needed to satisfy the test + KR.\n\nLet me re-read the task title and goal once more, very carefully:\n\n\"让 pibuilder 产出单文件内聚的 pi 定制化规范产物\"\n\n\"按 spec（task2）落地 KR3.1：pibuilder 产出 pi 定制化规范产物——pi agent 运行时所需的所有提示词内聚在单文件内，被 pi 以标准规范化定制开发语言引用使用。将「主 prompt 文件 + 多个 skill 文件散落（按路径引用）」改为「单文件内聚」：每个 cmd 的 pibuilder 产物把 skill/loop 内容内联进单个 .md 产物（而非散落文件 + 路径引用），可被 pi 直接加载执行。\"\n\nSo the core change: \"每个 cmd 的 pibuilder 产物把 skill/loop 内容内联进单个 .md 产物\". Each command's pibuilder product inlines skill/loop content into a single .md product.\n\nSo for plan: the plan_prompt.md (single .md) should inline the skill/loop content (grilling, tdd, etc.) instead of path-referencing scattered skill files.\n\nThis matches the boundary test: grilling content inline in plan --dry-run (which prints the plan instance).\n\nNow the KR1 note about \"method 自包含\" — I think this is clarifying that the METHOD is also self-contained (the command SOP is already there), and it's a clarification that \"单文件内聚\" doesn't conflict with the pi skills mechanism for on-demand skills. But the PRIMARY product that gets inlined is the instance (the single .md that pi loads).\n\nActually, re-reading: \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method）\".\n\nHmm. This clearly says method = self-contained with key loop/skill content inlined into method.\n\nBut then the boundary test checks grilling in the instance (plan --dry-run output).\n\nWait, let me reconsider whether PlanDryRun should print method + instance. Let me check the other dry-run functions (doing, easy).\n\nActually, maybe the cleanest solution that satisfies BOTH the KR note AND the test:\n1. Inline grilling (and other key skills) content into the METHOD (system prompt).\n2. ALSO inline grilling into the instance, OR change dry-run to print method + instance.\n\nLet me check what `doing --dry-run` and `easy --dry-run` currently print, and check the other tests (task10.py only tests plan, but the KR mentions plan/doing/easy).\n\nActually, the task10.py test ONLY tests `plan --dry-run`. So I only strictly need to satisfy the plan dry-run test + BuildPlan error. But the KR also mentions BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop. And the doing_check will check the format.\n\nLet me check the doing_check gate to understand what it validates.\n\nLet me look at the tools_doing_check / tools.go, and the doing tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_w0tVYbkIZIiIuBI7TTS47376","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/cmd/tools.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_03tf00DBQykze0KMHKMT9882","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/handler/doing.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_xNWIA7vDFvgRkQj8ZfeK0356","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/handler/easy.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2337,"output":4914,"cacheRead":72576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4753,"totalTokens":79827,"cost":{"input":0.0010165950000000001,"output":0.00427518,"cacheRead":0.000263088,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005554863}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913888306,"responseId":"b11a060c-4371-4d7f-829b-2f51a6d29109","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_w0tVYbkIZIiIuBI7TTS47376","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package cmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n)\n\n// NewToolsCmd creates the tools parent command\n// This is the meta-skill system for Rick, primarily used by AI agents.\n// AI agents invoke `rick tools --help` to discover available tools and\n// decide which commands to run during the learning phase.\nfunc NewToolsCmd() *cobra.Command {\n\ttoolsCmd := &cobra.Command{\n\t\tUse:   \"tools\",\n\t\tShort: \"Meta-skill tools for validating and managing Rick workflows\",\n\t\tLong: `rick tools provides a set of validation and management commands for Rick workflows.\n\nThese commands are primarily used by AI agents during the learning phase.\nAn AI agent reads 'rick tools --help' to discover all available tools,\nthen decides which commands to invoke to complete its work.\n\nAvailable subcommands:\n  init-pi         Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + subagent extension\n  learning_check  Validate the learning directory structure for a job (incl. loops/skills format)\n  dream_check     Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/ (incl. loops/skills format)\n`,\n\t\tRunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n\t\t\treturn cmd.Help()\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\ttoolsCmd.AddCommand(NewInitPiCmd())\n\ttoolsCmd.AddCommand(NewThemeCmd())\n\ttoolsCmd.AddCommand(NewLearningCheckCmd())\n\ttoolsCmd.AddCommand(NewDreamCheckCmd())\n\n\treturn toolsCmd\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913941536},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_03tf00DBQykze0KMHKMT9882","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package handler\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/builder\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\n)\n\n// Doing executes the complete doing workflow. Scheduling is now delegated to\n// pi's workflowScript orchestration (parent single-writer + runs.run with await),\n// and the gate is a deterministic rick-side script run after the pi session\n// settles. rick's retry loop is only a safety net: it regenerates an\n// orchestration of the remaining pending tasks on each attempt, bounded by\n// cfg.MaxRetries.\nfunc Doing(jobID string, opts Options) error {\n\tcfg, err := config.LoadConfig()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load config: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to get rick directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tjobDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID)\n\tplanDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"plan\")\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"doing\")\n\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(jobDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job directory not found: %s\", jobDir)\n\t}\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(planDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"plan directory not found: %s\", planDir)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(doingDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create doing directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tif opts.Verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Job directory: %s\\n\", jobDir)\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Plan directory: %s\\n\", planDir)\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Doing directory: %s\\n\", doingDir)\n\t}\n\n\t// Initial tasks.json draft: builder scans plan/task*.md (all pending).\n\tif err := builder.EnsureTasksJSON(doingDir, planDir); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to initialize tasks.json: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tmaxRetries := cfg.MaxRetries\n\tif maxRetries <= 0 {\n\t\tmaxRetries = 3\n\t}\n\n\tpiRuntime := runtime.NewPiRuntime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...)\n\n\tfor attempt := 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++ {\n\t\tif opts.Verbose {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Attempt %d/%d\\n\", attempt, maxRetries)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// builder regenerates an orchestration of only the remaining pending\n\t\t// tasks (completed tasks are filtered out at generation time).\n\t\tpromptFile, method, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(doingDir, planDir, rickDir, jobID)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build doing prompt: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t_, _, err = piRuntime.Run(method, promptFile, cfg)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] pi run did not settle (attempt %d/%d): %v\\n\", attempt, maxRetries, err)\n\t\t\tif attempt < maxRetries {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pi run failed after %d attempts: %w\", maxRetries, err)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Deterministic gate after the session settles (agent_settled).\n\t\tif gateErr := runDoingGate(rickDir, doingDir); gateErr != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] gate failed (attempt %d/%d): %v\\n\", attempt, maxRetries, gateErr)\n\t\t\tif attempt < maxRetries {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"doing gate failed after %d attempts: %w\", maxRetries, gateErr)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Job %s execution completed!\\n\", jobID)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job execution incomplete after %d attempts\", maxRetries)\n}\n\n// runDoingGate runs the deterministic rick-side gate script:\n// python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doingDir>. Exit non-zero = gate\n// failure (unparseable tasks.json / zombie running / success without commit_hash).\nfunc runDoingGate(rickDir, doingDir string) error {\n\thelper := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\", \"rick-gates\", \"helper.py\")\n\tcmd := exec.Command(\"python3\", helper, doingDir)\n\tout, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tmsg := strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n\t\tif msg == \"\" {\n\t\t\tmsg = err.Error()\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s\", msg)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// DoingDryRun generates and prints the doing prompt (with the pi workflowScript\n// orchestration) without executing it.\nfunc DoingDryRun(jobID string) error {\n\tif jobID == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"[DRY-RUN] No job ID provided\")\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to get rick dir: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tplanDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"plan\")\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(planDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\tdoingDirFallback := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\t\tif _, e := os.Stat(filepath.Join(doingDirFallback, \"requirement.md\")); e == nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] %s is an easy mode job (no plan/). Use: rick doing --easy --dry-run\\n\", jobID)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] plan directory not found: %s\\n\", planDir)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\n\tpromptFile, _, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(doingDir, planDir, rickDir, jobID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to generate prompt: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tcontent, err := os.ReadFile(promptFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to read prompt file: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] Doing prompt:\\n\\n\")\n\tfmt.Println(string(content))\n\treturn nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913941536},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_xNWIA7vDFvgRkQj8ZfeK0356","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package handler\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/rand\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/builder\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\n)\n\n// EasyDryRun prints the easy prompt without creating any job or calling pi\n// (migrated from cmd.runEasyDryRun).\nfunc EasyDryRun(requirement, ctxPath string) error {\n\tif requirement == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"requirement cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to get rick dir: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\t_, content, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().BuildEasy(requirement, map[string]string{\n\t\t\"rick_dir\":  rickDir,\n\t\t\"doing_dir\": filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", \"job_N\", \"doing\"),\n\t\t\"ctx_path\":  ctxPath,\n\t\t\"job_id\":    \"job_N\",\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to generate prompt: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(\"[DRY-RUN] Easy prompt:\")\n\tfmt.Println()\n\tfmt.Println(content)\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// Easy creates a new job and starts an easy interactive session (migrated from\n// cmd.runEasyMode). Interactive requirement prompting stays in the CLI layer.\nfunc Easy(requirement, ctxPath string, opts Options) error {\n\tif requirement == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"requirement cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to get rick directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// --ctx: guard against overwriting existing context\n\tif ctxPath != \"\" {\n\t\tif err := validateCtxInheritance(rickDir, ctxPath); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tjobID, err := workspace.NextJobID()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to determine next job ID: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tcfg, err := config.LoadConfig()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load config: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn StartEasySession(jobID, requirement, rickDir, cfg, ctxPath, opts)\n}\n\n// validateCtxInheritance checks that:\n// 1. The target ctxPath exists and looks like a .rick directory.\n// 2. The local .rick does NOT already have loops/ or skills/ (to prevent accidental overwrite).\nfunc validateCtxInheritance(localRickDir, ctxPath string) error {\n\t// Verify the source ctx path exists\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(ctxPath); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"--ctx path does not exist: %s\", ctxPath)\n\t}\n\t// Verify local .rick has no existing loops/ or skills/\n\tfor _, name := range []string{\"loops\", \"skills\"} {\n\t\tp := filepath.Join(localRickDir, name)\n\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(p); err == nil && info.IsDir() {\n\t\t\tentries, _ := os.ReadDir(p)\n\t\t\tif len(entries) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"local context already exists (%s). Remove it first or omit --ctx\", p)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// ResumeEasy resumes an existing easy session by job ID (migrated from\n// cmd.resumeEasyMode).\nfunc ResumeEasy(jobID string, opts Options) error {\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to get rick directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(doingDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job %s does not exist or has no doing directory\", jobID)\n\t}\n\n\tsessionID, err := loadSessionID(doingDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"no session found for job %s: %w\", jobID, err)\n\t}\n\n\tcfg, err := config.LoadConfig()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load config: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tfmt.Printf(\"Job ID: %s\\n\", jobID)\n\tfmt.Printf(\"Resuming session: %s\\n\", sessionID)\n\n\tif err := runtime.CallCLI(opts.Verbose, cfg, \"\", runtime.ModeInteractive, \"--session-id\", sessionID); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"session resume failed: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Update tasks.json timestamp on resume so dream sees the latest run\n\tif err := writeEasyTasksJSON(doingDir); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] failed to write tasks.json: %v\\n\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// StartEasySession runs the full easy session flow for a new job (migrated from\n// cmd.startEasySession).\nfunc StartEasySession(jobID, requirement, rickDir string, cfg *config.Config, ctxPath string, opts Options) error {\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(doingDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create doing directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Write requirement\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"requirement.md\"), []byte(requirement), 0644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write requirement: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Generate session UUID and persist\n\tsessionID, err := generateUUID()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to generate session ID: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := saveSessionID(doingDir, sessionID); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save session ID: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tmainFile, _, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveEasyPrompt(jobID, requirement, rickDir, ctxPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to generate easy prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tfmt.Printf(\"Job ID: %s\\n\", jobID)\n\tfmt.Printf(\"Session ID: %s\\n\", sessionID)\n\tfmt.Println(\"🤖 Starting Easy interactive session...\")\n\n\tif err := runtime.CallCLI(opts.Verbose, cfg, mainFile, runtime.ModeInteractive, \"--session-id\", sessionID); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"easy session failed: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Write synthetic tasks.json so dream can discover this job\n\tif err := writeEasyTasksJSON(doingDir); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] failed to write tasks.json: %v\\n\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// saveSessionID persists the session UUID to doingDir/session_id.\nfunc saveSessionID(doingDir, sessionID string) error {\n\treturn os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"session_id\"), []byte(sessionID), 0644)\n}\n\n// loadSessionID reads the session UUID from doingDir/session_id.\nfunc loadSessionID(doingDir string) (string, error) {\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"session_id\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\treturn string(data), nil\n}\n\n// writeEasyTasksJSON writes a synthetic tasks.json so dream can discover this\n// easy job. Easy mode has no task breakdown, so we write a single\n// \"easy_session\" task as success.\nfunc writeEasyTasksJSON(doingDir string) error {\n\tnow := time.Now()\n\ttasksJSON := map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\"version\":    \"1.0\",\n\t\t\"created_at\": now,\n\t\t\"updated_at\": now,\n\t\t\"tasks\": []map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\"task_id\":      \"easy_session\",\n\t\t\t\t\"task_name\":    \"Easy Mode Session\",\n\t\t\t\t\"task_file\":    \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\"status\":       \"success\",\n\t\t\t\t\"dependencies\": []string{},\n\t\t\t\t\"attempts\":     1,\n\t\t\t\t\"created_at\":   now,\n\t\t\t\t\"updated_at\":   now,\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\tdata, err := json.MarshalIndent(tasksJSON, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"tasks.json\"), data, 0644)\n}\n\n// generateUUID generates a random UUID (v4).\nfunc generateUUID() (string, error) {\n\tvar b [16]byte\n\tif _, err := rand.Read(b[:]); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tb[6] = (b[6] & 0x0f) | 0x40 // version 4\n\tb[8] = (b[8] & 0x3f) | 0x80 // variant bits\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%08x-%04x-%04x-%04x-%012x\",\n\t\tb[0:4], b[4:6], b[6:8], b[8:10], b[10:16]), nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913941536}]}
