{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Interesting! The grep output is confusing. It says:\n```\n=== tdd-zh ===\n0\nMISSING\n=== testing-anti-patterns-zh ===\n0\nMISSING\n```\n\nWait, that's weird. `grep -c '{{' file` outputs `0` (count 0) and then `|| echo \"MISSING\"` — but grep -c returns exit code 1 when count is 0, so `|| echo MISSING` fires. So the files exist but have 0 occurrences of `{{`. So:\n- tdd-zh.md: 0 `{{`\n- testing-anti-patterns-zh.md: 0 `{{`\n- grilling.md: 0 `{{`\n- doing_loop.md: 4 `{{` (these are `{{domain_dir}}` and `{{debug_skill_path}}` which get replaced)\n- debug_skill.md: 1 `{{`\n- learning_loop.md: 27 `{{`\n- gen-skill.md: 0 `{{`\n- gen-loop.md: 2 `{{`\n- gen-domain.md: 0 `{{`\n- import_ctx.md: 11 `{{`\n\nSo grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh have NO `{{` placeholders. Good. So I can safely inline them into plan without creating unreplaced `{{`.\n\nNow let me finalize my approach.\n\n**Decision**: \n1. Add `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name string) (string, error)` to prompt/manager.go.\n2. In `builder/pibuilder.go` `BuildPlan`: read grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh via `ReadEmbeddedSkill`. On error, return error (wrapped to include name). Then inline the content into the instance.\n\nFor inlining, I'll modify the plan.md template to add an inline section. But wait, that would require also updating `GeneratePlanPrompt` in prompt package to set the new variable (to avoid breaking `TestGeneratePlanPrompt_NoUnreplacedVars`).\n\nActually, let me think about a cleaner approach that avoids touching the plan.md template AND avoids breaking prompt package tests.\n\n**Alternative approach: Post-process in builder.**\n\nIn `BuildPlan`, after `b.Build()` produces the instance, append the inline skill sections to the instance string directly. This doesn't touch plan.md at all, so `GeneratePlanPrompt` (prompt package) stays untouched and its tests stay green.\n\nBut wait — the KR says \"单文件含 pi 可识别的结构化引用（agent frontmatter / skill 内联段）\". So the inline sections should be \"skill 内联段\" — recognizable structured references. I can append:\n\n```markdown\n---\n\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\n\n### skill:grilling\n\n<grilling content>\n\n### skill:tdd\n\n<tdd content>\n\n### skill:testing-anti-patterns\n\n<testing content>\n```\n\nThis is clean and doesn't require template changes.\n\nBut then there's redundancy: the SOP step 4 still says \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\" where X is a placeholder path. And I'd ALSO inline the content. The test comment says \"而非仅 `skill_grilling.md` 路径引用\" — so having BOTH the path reference AND inline content is fine (it's \"not just path reference\"). The test just checks the content is there.\n\nActually, wait — but the KR says \"散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\". To truly reduce path references, I could change `grilling_skill_path` from a path placeholder to point at the inline section, or remove it. But the SOP text \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\" is the trigger language that task11 migrates.\n\nHmm. Let me think about what's most correct and clean.\n\nActually, I think the cleanest and most faithful approach is:\n\n1. Modify plan.md to inline the grilling/tdd/testing-anti-patterns content directly in a dedicated section, replacing the path references in the SOP with references to the inline sections.\n\nBut that changes the trigger language a bit. Let me look at the exact SOP text again:\n\n```\n4. **grilling 追问**：加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`），对用户需求逐问追问...\n```\n\nThe \"触发语言\" here is \"加载 skill:grilling\" (load skill:grilling). The \"（路径：X）\" is the path reference, which is what this task is about (reducing path references). So I could change it to:\n\n```\n4. **grilling 追问**：加载 skill:grilling（内容已内联至下方「内联技能」节），对用户需求逐问追问...\n```\n\nBut that's borderline. Let me be conservative and keep the SOP text as-is, and just ADD the inline content section. This way:\n- The trigger language is unchanged (task11's job).\n- The path reference still exists but the content is ALSO inlined (so pi doesn't strictly need the path).\n- The test passes (grilling content inline).\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the whole thing once more. Let me re-read the key result 3:\n\n\"产物可被 pi 加载：单文件含 pi 可识别的结构化引用（agent frontmatter / skill 内联段），不依赖散落文件路径拼装\"\n\nSo the single file should contain \"skill 内联段\" (skill inline sections) — this is the \"pi 可识别的结构化引用\". So I should add a clearly-structured inline section.\n\nI think the cleanest approach that satisfies everything without over-engineering:\n\n**Modify plan.md template** to add an inline skills section at the end, with variables for each skill's content. Then update both `GeneratePlanPrompt` (prompt pkg) and `BuildPlan` (builder pkg) to populate those variables.\n\nBut wait, there's a concern: `GeneratePlanPrompt` in prompt package currently sets `grilling_skill_path` to a placeholder path. If I add `{{grilling_content}}` to plan.md, I need `GeneratePlanPrompt` to also set it (or else `TestGeneratePlanPrompt_NoUnreplacedVars` fails).\n\nActually, this is getting complicated. Let me go with the simpler post-processing approach in the builder, which:\n\n1. Doesn't touch plan.md (so prompt package tests remain green).\n2. Adds inline content in the builder's BuildPlan output.\n3. Uses ReadEmbeddedSkill.\n\nThis satisfies the test and most of the KR. The \"skill 内联段\" structure I add in the builder output IS the \"pi 可识别的结构化引用\".\n\nBut hold on — there's a subtlety with the exception test (task10.py test 3):\n\n```go\n_, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().BuildPlan(\"dry-run requirement\", map[string]string{\n    \"rick_dir\":     rickDir,\n    \"job_plan_dir\": jobPlanDir,\n})\nif err != nil { fmt.Printf(\"ERR:%v\\n\", err) ... }\n```\n\nWhen grilling.md is deleted and rebuilt, `BuildPlan` must return error containing \"grilling\". So in `BuildPlan`, I must call `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` and if it errors, return the error. This is straightforward.\n\nNow, what about the `SavePlanPrompt` path (non-dry-run)? It calls `prompt.GeneratePlanPromptFile`, which still writes skill files and uses path references. The task says \"pibuilder 的 BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop 产出的主产物\" — so the main product includes both Build* (dry-run) and Save* (file). But the test only checks BuildPlan (dry-run) + plan --dry-run.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the KR1: \"pibuilder 的 BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop 产出的主产物把关键 skill/loop 内容内联\". The \"Build*\" methods return (method, instance, err). The \"Save*\" methods write files. The test focuses on Build* (dry-run).\n\nGiven the test only checks plan --dry-run and BuildPlan, and given the KR says \"BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop\", I should apply the same treatment to all four Build* methods (and ideally their Save* counterparts). But to keep changes focused and avoid breaking existing tests, I'll:\n\n1. `BuildPlan`: inline grilling + tdd-zh + testing-anti-patterns-zh into instance.\n2. `BuildDoing`: inline doing_loop (already done via renderDoingLoop, but switch to ReadEmbeddedSkill with error) + debug_skill? Actually doing_loop is already inlined. The key loop is doing_loop. Let me switch `renderDoingLoop` to use ReadEmbeddedSkill and return error.\n3. `BuildEasy`: inline grilling + debug_skill + learning_loop + doing_loop into instance.\n4. `BuildHumanLoop`: it delegates to GenerateHumanLoopPrompt. The sense/think/research/exporter are already \"inlined\" as templates (the main prompt inlines the subagent prompts' content? No, it references paths). Hmm.\n\nActually, let me focus. The task10 test ONLY checks plan. The KR lists all four, but the test is the acceptance gate. Let me do a thorough but clean job:\n\n- Add `ReadEmbeddedSkill` to prompt package.\n- In `BuildPlan`, inline grilling (required by test), tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh (referenced in plan SOP).\n- In `BuildDoing`/`BuildEasy`, switch `renderDoingLoop` to use `ReadEmbeddedSkill` (with error propagation) instead of `LoadCoreSkills`.\n- In `BuildEasy`, inline grilling content (via ReadEmbeddedSkill).\n- `BuildHumanLoop` — the sense/think/research/exporter are agent prompts written as files. The main sense_loop prompt references think/research/exporter agent paths. This is a different structure (sub-agent orchestration). I'll leave BuildHumanLoop mostly as-is but could inline the skills. Actually, given the test doesn't check it and it's a different structure, I'll do minimal: ensure it still works.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to touch `renderDoingLoop`. The current `renderDoingLoop` uses `LoadCoreSkills` which returns empty string on missing skill (logs warning). If I switch to `ReadEmbeddedSkill` and propagate error, the `BuildDoing`/`BuildEasy` signatures already return error, so it's clean.\n\nBut there's a risk: the doing_loop.md has 4 `{{` placeholders (`{{domain_dir}}` ×3, `{{debug_skill_path}}` ×1). After `renderDoingLoop` strips frontmatter and replaces `{{domain_dir}}` and `{{debug_skill_path}}`, there should be no `{{` left. Let me verify: doing_loop.md has 4 `{{`. The `renderDoingLoop` replaces `{{domain_dir}}` (appears how many times?) and `{{debug_skill_path}}`. Let me check.\n\nActually, from the doing_loop.md content I read, it has:\n- `{{domain_dir}}` appears in Step 0.1 (twice: \"读取 `{{domain_dir}}` 下\" and \"搜索 `{{domain_dir}}/bugs.md`\"), Step 0.2 \"读取 `loops_context`\" (no), DEBUG step \"搜索 `{{domain_dir}}/bugs.md`\".\n- `{{debug_skill_path}}` appears in DEBUG step \"加载 skill 文件：`{{debug_skill_path}}`\".\n\nSo 3× `{{domain_dir}}` + 1× `{{debug_skill_path}}` = 4 `{{`. All replaced by renderDoingLoop. Good.\n\nBut wait, the doing.md template itself doesn't contain `{{domain_dir}}` or `{{debug_skill_path}}` — those are inside doing_loop.md which is embedded via `{{doing_loop_content}}`. Since `renderDoingLoop` already substitutes them before setting `doing_loop_content`, the final output has no `{{`