t wait — there's a Go embed subtlety: `//go:embed templates/skills` embeds the whole directory. If grilling.md is deleted, the embed just won't include it. `skillsFS.ReadFile` will return `os.ErrNotExist` (or `fs.ErrNotExist`). My `ReadEmbeddedSkill` returns error wrapping it. \n\nNow, the order matters: I read the inline skills BEFORE or AFTER building. Let me read BEFORE building, so that if grilling is missing, BuildPlan returns error early (doesn't produce partial output). Actually, the test just checks the error is returned; order doesn't matter for the test. But reading before build is cleaner.\n\nActually, wait — there's another consideration. The `BuildPlan` currently reads the template via `p.manager().LoadTemplate(\"plan\")`. The plan.md template has `{{grilling_skill_path}}` etc. Those still get replaced with placeholder paths. The instance will contain \"skill_grilling\" (the placeholder path `<tmp>/rick-plan-prompts/skill_grilling.md`). So the output will have BOTH the path reference AND the inline content. That satisfies the test (inline content present) and the existing structure (path still there).\n\nBut the KR says \"散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\". With my approach, the path reference is still there but content is also inlined. This is \"not just path\" (满足 test comment \"而非仅路径引用\"). \"引用下降\" — well, the references haven't decreased, but the content is inlined. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider. To truly reduce path references, I could change the placeholder `grilling_skill_path` value to point at the inline section instead of a file path. But the SOP text says \"（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\".\n\nActually, you know what, I think the cleanest faithful approach is to MODIFY the plan.md template to properly inline. Let me reconsider Option A more carefully.\n\nThe issue with Option A is I'd need to update `GeneratePlanPrompt` and `GeneratePlanPromptFile` in the prompt package too, to keep their tests green. But actually, that's not a bad thing — it makes the prompt package's generators also produce inlined output, which is MORE consistent with the KR.\n\nBut wait — there's a risk. `GeneratePlanPromptFile` is called by `SavePlanPrompt` (builder) for the non-dry-run path. If I change it to inline skills, the skill files are still written (the existing test checks that). But the actual non-dry-run `rick plan` would now inline skills into plan_prompt.md AND still write skill files. That's fine.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about what's the MINIMAL change to pass the test and satisfy the KR, with the LEAST risk of breaking existing tests.\n\nThe task10.py test checks:\n1. `plan --dry-run` → no `{{`, >0 lines.\n2. `plan --dry-run` → contains \"Grilling\" or \"结构化追问\".\n3. `BuildPlan` → error with \"grilling\" when grilling.md deleted.\n\n`go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/... -v` must pass (existing tests + any new tests I add).\n\nThe simplest approach: **Option B (post-process in builder)**, which:\n- Doesn't touch plan.md (no risk to prompt pkg tests).\n- Only modifies `builder/pibuilder.go` + adds `ReadEmbeddedSkill` to prompt pkg.\n- Satisfies all 3 test assertions.\n\nThis is clearly the lowest-risk approach. Let me go with Option B, but make it clean.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the \"method 自包含\" requirement once more, because it's in KR1 and I want to be faithful.\n\nKR1 note: \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method）\".\n\nHmm, \"method（system prompt）这一份自包含\". The `commandMethod` function builds the method (system prompt). Currently the method for plan is just the SOP one-liner. The \"关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method\" suggests the method should inline the loop/skill content.\n\nBut the test checks `plan --dry-run` output = instance (not method). So if I inline into method only, the test fails.\n\nUnless... the handler's `PlanDryRun` should print method + instance. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, re-reading the test's \"正常路径\": \"预期 = 输出为单个连贯 prompt（行数 > 