{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, I now have a comprehensive understanding. The `debug_skill.md` has `{{sense_skill_path}}` (1 occurrence). So if I inline debug_skill content, I'd need to replace that. But that's part of the doing/easy flow, not plan.\n\nFor the plan command, the key skills are grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh (all 0 `{{`).\n\nNow let me design the final implementation cleanly.\n\n**Step 1: Add `ReadEmbeddedSkill` to `internal/prompt/manager.go`.**\n\n```go\n// skillPath maps a skill name to its embedded path under templates/skills/.\nfunc skillPath(name string) string {\n\treturn \"templates/skills/\" + name + \".md\"\n}\n\n// ReadEmbeddedSkill reads a single embedded skill's raw content by name.\n// It is the cross-package accessor for the unexported skillsFS (builder 是独立包，\n// skillsFS 未导出，必须经本导出函数访问)。Missing skill returns an error rather\n// than silently producing empty content.\nfunc ReadEmbeddedSkill(name string) (string, error) {\n\tcontent, err := skillsFS.ReadFile(skillPath(name))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"embedded skill %q not found: %w\", name, err)\n\t}\n\treturn string(content), nil\n}\n```\n\nThen refactor `LoadCoreSkills` to use `skillPath` for consistency:\n```go\nfunc LoadCoreSkills(names []string) string {\n\tvar parts []string\n\tfor _, name := range names {\n\t\tcontent, err := skillsFS.ReadFile(skillPath(name))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tlog.Printf(...)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\t...\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps `LoadCoreSkills` behavior identical (just refactored to use skillPath).\n\n**Step 2: Add a helper in builder to build inline skill sections.**\n\nIn `pibuilder.go`, add a helper:\n```go\n// renderInlineSkills reads embedded skills via prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill and renders\n// a single-file cohesive \"skill 内联段\" section. Missing skill returns error.\nfunc renderInlineSkills(skills []string) (string, error) {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor _, name := range skills {\n\t\tcontent, err := prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n### skill:\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(name)\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stripYAMLFrontmatter(content))\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String(), nil\n}\n```\n\nWait, should I strip the YAML frontmatter? The grilling.md doesn't have frontmatter (it starts with `# Skill: Grilling`). The tdd-zh.md has frontmatter `---\\nname:...\\n---`. For the inline section, stripping frontmatter makes sense (it's a method content, not a standalone file). Actually, let me check: grilling.md starts with `# Skill: Grilling（结构化追问协议）` — no frontmatter. tdd-zh.md starts with frontmatter. testing-anti-patterns-zh.md starts with `# 测试反模式` — no frontmatter.\n\nSo for tdd-zh, I should strip frontmatter to avoid including the YAML `---` in the inline section (which could confuse pi). Actually, stripping frontmatter is consistent with how `renderDoingLoop` strips frontmatter from doing_loop.md.\n\nBut wait — does stripping matter for the test? The test greps for \"Grilling|结构化追问\". grilling.md has no frontmatter, so it doesn't matter for grilling. For tdd-zh, frontmatter has `name: test-driven-development` — if I don't strip, the inline section would have a stray `---` block. That's harmless but ugly. I'll strip frontmatter for cleanliness.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether to strip. The `stripYAMLFrontmatter` function is defined in both `prompt` (easy_prompt.go) and `builder` (pibuilder.go). In builder, it's:\n```go\nfunc stripYAMLFrontmatter(s string) string {\n\tif !strings.HasPrefix(s, \"---\\n\") {\n\t\treturn s\n\t}\n\trest := s[4:]\n\tidx := strings.Index(rest, \"\\n---\\n\")\n\tif idx < 0 {\n\t\treturn s\n\t}\n\treturn strings.TrimLeft(rest[idx+5:], \"\\n\")\n}\n```\n\nThis works fine. I'll use it.\n\n**Step 3: Modify `BuildPlan` to inline skills.**\n\n```go\nfunc (p *PIBuilder) BuildPlan(requirement string, params map[string]string) (method string, instance string, err error) {\n\tif requirement == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"requirement cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\n\trickDir := getParam(params, \"rick_dir\")\n\tjobPlanDir := getParam(params, \"job_plan_dir\")\n\tif jobPlanDir == \"\" {\n\t\tjobPlanDir = filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", \"job_N\", \"plan\")\n\t}\n\n\ttmpl, err := p.manager().LoadTemplate(\"plan\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load plan template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// 单文件内聚：关键 skill 内容内联进主产物（而非散落路径引用）。\n\t// 缺内联源时返回 error（非 panic / 非静默空内容）。\n\tinlineSkills, err := renderInlineSkills([]string{\"grilling\", \"tdd-zh\", \"testing-anti-patterns-zh\"})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to inline plan skills: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tb := prompt.NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"loops_context\", ...)\n\t...\n\tb.SetVariable(\"inline_skills\", inlineSkills)\n\n\tinstance, err = b.Build()\n\t...\n}\n```\n\nBut wait — this requires adding `{{inline_skills}}` to plan.md template. And that would break `GeneratePlanPrompt` (prompt package) unless I also set it there.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. The plan.md template is shared between:\n1. `GeneratePlanPrompt` / `GeneratePlanPromptFile` (prompt package)\n2. `BuildPlan` / `SavePlanPrompt` (builder package)\n\nIf I add `{{inline_skills}}` to plan.md, both must set it.\n\nOption A: Add `{{inline_skills}}` to plan.md, and update `GeneratePlanPrompt` + `GeneratePlanPromptFile` to also inline skills (using the new ReadEmbeddedSkill). This is actually MORE faithful — the prompt package's generators should also produce the inlined output.\n\nBut wait, `GeneratePlanPromptFile` writes skill files AND is used by `SavePlanPrompt`. If I inline skills there too, that's fine — the skill files are still written (the existing test `TestGeneratePlanPromptFile_WritesGrillingSkillFile` checks the file is written). And `TestGeneratePlanPrompt_HasGrillingSkillPath` checks \"skill_grilling\" in the output — if I keep the `grilling_skill_path` variable AND add inline content, \"skill_grilling\" is still in the output. And `TestGeneratePlanPrompt_NoUnreplacedGrillingVar` checks `!Contains \"{{grilling_skill_path}}\"` — still satisfied. And `TestGeneratePlanPrompt_NoUnreplacedVars` checks no `{{` — so I must set `{{inline_skills}}` in `GeneratePlanPrompt` too.\n\nHmm, but this is getting into modifying the prompt package's generators too, which is a broader change. The task10 scope is \"pibuilder 产出单文件内聚\". The prompt package's `GeneratePlanPrompt` etc. are \"底层能力\" from task5.\n\nActually, let me reconsider Option B: **Don't modify plan.md. Post-process the instance in the builder.**\n\nIn `BuildPlan`:\n```go\ninstance, err = b.Build()\nif err != nil { ... }\n\n// 单文件内聚：关键 skill 内容内联。\ninlineSkills, err := renderInlineSkills([]string{\"grilling\", \"tdd-zh\", \"testing-anti-patterns-zh\"})\nif err != nil { return ..., fmt.Errorf(\"...grilling...\") }\ninstance += \"\\n\\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\\n\" + inlineSkills\n```\n\nThis is simpler, doesn't touch plan.md, and doesn't affect prompt package tests. The inline content is appended as a clearly-structured section.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: the exception test expects error message to contain \"grilling\". With `renderInlineSkills([]string{\"grilling\", ...})`, when grilling is missing, `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` returns error \"embedded skill \\\"grilling\\\" not found: ...\". The wrapper \"failed to inline plan skills: ...\" → contains \"grilling\". Good.\n\nWait, but actually there's an even subtler issue. The task10.py test runs the probe against the ACTUAL repo after deleting grilling.md. The `ReadEmbeddedSkill` uses `skillsFS` which is the embedded FS. When grilling.md is deleted and `go build` re-runs, the embed will NOT include grilling.md, so `skillsFS.ReadFile(\"templates/skills/grilling.md\")` returns error. \n\nBut wait — there's a Go embed subtlety: `//go:embed templates/skills` embeds the whole directory. If grilling.md is deleted, the embed just won't include it. `skillsFS.ReadFile` will return `os.ErrNotExist` (or `fs.ErrNotExist`). My `ReadEmbeddedSkill` returns error wrapping it. \n\nNow, the order matters: I read the inline skills BEFORE or AFTER building. Let me read BEFORE building, so that if grilling is missing, BuildPlan returns error early (doesn't produce partial output). Actually, the test just checks the error is returned; order doesn't matter for the test. But reading before build is cleaner.\n\nActually, wait — there's another consideration. The `BuildPlan` currently reads the template via `p.manager().LoadTemplate(\"plan\")`. The plan.md template has `{{grilling_skill_path}}` etc. Those still get replaced with placeholder paths. The instance will contain \"skill_grilling\" (the placeholder path `<tmp>/rick-plan-prompts/skill_grilling.md`). So the output will have BOTH the path reference AND the inline content. That satisfies the test (inline content present) and the existing structure (path still there).\n\nBut the KR says \"散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\". With my approach, the path reference is still there but content is also inlined. This is \"not just path\" (满足 test comment \"而非仅路径引用\"). \"引用下降\" — well, the references haven't decreased, but the content is inlined. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider. To truly reduce path references, I could change the placeholder `grilling_skill_path` value to point at the inline section instead of a file path. But the SOP text says \"（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\".\n\nActually, you know what, I think the cleanest faithful approach is to MODIFY the plan.md template to properly inline. Let me reconsider Option A more carefully.\n\nThe issue with Option A is I'd need to update `GeneratePlanPrompt` and `GeneratePlanPromptFile` in the prompt package too, to keep their tests green. But actually, that's not a bad thing — it makes the prompt package's generators also produce inlined output, which is MORE consistent with the KR.\n\nBut wait — there's a risk. `GeneratePlanPromptFile` is called by `SavePlanPrompt` (builder) for the non-dry-run path. If I change it to inline skills, the skill files are still written (the existing test checks that). But the actual non-dry-run `rick plan` would now inline skills into plan_prompt.md AND still write skill files. That's fine.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about what's the MINIMAL change to pass the test and satisfy the KR, with the LEAST risk of breaking existing tests.\n\nThe task10.py test checks:\n1. `plan --dry-run` → no `{{`, >0 lines.\n2. `plan --dry-run` → contains \"Grilling\" or \"结构化追问\".\n3. `BuildPlan` → error with \"grilling\" when grilling.md deleted.\n\n`go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/... -v` must pass (existing tests + any new tests I add).\n\nThe simplest approach: **Option B (post-process in builder)**, which:\n- Doesn't touch plan.md (no risk to prompt pkg tests).\n- Only modifies `builder/pibuilder.go` + adds `ReadEmbeddedSkill` to prompt pkg.\n- Satisfies all 3 test assertions.\n\nThis is clearly the lowest-risk approach. Let me go with Option B, but make it clean.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the \"method 自包含\" requirement once more, because it's in KR1 and I want to be faithful.\n\nKR1 note: \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method）\".\n\nHmm, \"method（system prompt）这一份自包含\". The `commandMethod` function builds the method (system prompt). Currently the method for plan is just the SOP one-liner. The \"关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method\" suggests the method should inline the loop/skill content.\n\nBut the test checks `plan --dry-run` output = instance (not method). So if I inline into method only, the test fails.\n\nUnless... the handler's `PlanDryRun` should print method + instance. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, re-reading the test's \"正常路径\": \"预期 = 输出为单个连贯 prompt（行数 > 0），`{{` 计数 0\". And \"边界\": grep grilling content. The test treats `plan --dry-run` output as \"单个连贯 prompt\" (single coherent prompt).\n\nThe task goal says \"--dry-run 输出完整单文件内容\". \"完整单文件\" = the complete single file. If the \"单文件\" = method + instance combined, then dry-run should print both.\n\nHmm. Let me look at what the current `plan --dry-run` prints vs what the actual pi receives:\n- Non-dry-run: `SavePlanPrompt` → writes `plan_prompt.md` (instance), and `runtime.CallCLI` receives the prompt file. The method goes via `--append-system-prompt`. So pi receives: system prompt (method) + user prompt file (instance).\n\nFor dry-run to show \"完整单文件内容\", it should show what pi loads. But the method goes via a separate flag.\n\nI think the simplest interpretation that satisfies the test: the \"主产物\" = the instance (plan_prompt.md), and grilling content should be inlined there. The \"method 自包含\" note is about the method ALSO being self-contained (which it already is, being a SOP string).\n\nActually, let me just re-read the KR1 note ONE more time and parse it as a parenthetical clarification rather than a hard requirement:\n\n\"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\"\n\nParse: \"单文件内聚\" refers to [the fact that] method (system prompt) is self-contained (key loop/skill content inlined into method). On-demand skills (grilling/tdd etc.) still use pi skills mechanism. The two don't conflict.\n\nHmm wait, but then grilling is listed as an \"执行期按需技能\" that \"仍走 pi skills 机制\". So grilling should NOT be inlined?? But the test requires grilling inline!\n\nThere's a genuine contradiction between the KR note's parenthetical and the test. The test is the authoritative acceptance gate (task10.py). And the task10.md's own 测试方法 section 2 explicitly says \"grilling skill 内容内联进主产物\".\n\nSo I'll follow the test and the task10.md 测试方法 (which is more specific and authoritative than the KR note's parenthetical