{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now let me make the edits. First, change `renderDoingLoop` to use `ReadEmbeddedSkill` and return error. Also add `renderInlineSkills` helper.\n\nLet me plan the edits:\n\n1. Replace `renderDoingLoop` function:\n```go\nfunc renderDoingLoop(domainDir, debugSkillPath string) (string, error) {\n\traw, err := prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"doing_loop\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tcontent := stripYAMLFrontmatter(raw)\n\tcontent = strings.ReplaceAll(content, \"{{domain_dir}}\", domainDir)\n\treturn strings.ReplaceAll(content, \"{{debug_skill_path}}\", debugSkillPath), nil\n}\n```\n\n2. Add `renderInlineSkills` helper after `stripYAMLFrontmatter` (or near renderDoingLoop):\n```go\n// renderInlineSkills reads embedded skills via prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill and renders\n// them as a single-file cohesive「skill 内联段」. Missing skill returns error.\nfunc renderInlineSkills(skills []string) (string, error) {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor _, name := range skills {\n\t\tcontent, err := prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n### skill:\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(name)\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stripYAMLFrontmatter(content))\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String(), nil\n}\n```\n\n3. Modify `BuildPlan` to inline skills. Let me see the current BuildPlan code (lines 250-275). I already have it from the earlier read. Let me make the edits.\n\nCurrent BuildPlan (from earlier):\n```go\nfunc (p *PIBuilder) BuildPlan(requirement string, params map[string]string) (method string, instance string, err error) {\n\tif requirement == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"requirement cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\n\trickDir := getParam(params, \"rick_dir\")\n\tjobPlanDir := getParam(params, \"job_plan_dir\")\n\tif jobPlanDir == \"\" {\n\t\tjobPlanDir = filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", \"job_N\", \"plan\")\n\t}\n\n\ttmpl, err := p.manager().LoadTemplate(\"plan\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load plan template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tb := prompt.NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"loops_context\", prompt.LoadLoopsContext(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"loops\")))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"domain_dir\", filepath.Join(rickDir, \"domain\"))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"user_requirement\", requirement)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"job_plan_dir\", jobPlanDir)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"rick_bin_path\", resolveRickBinPath())\n\tb.SetVariable(\"job_id\", extractJobID(jobPlanDir))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"grilling_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-prompts/skill_grilling.md\")\n\tb.SetVariable(\"tdd_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-tdd-zh-*.md\")\n\tb.SetVariable(\"testing_anti_patterns_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-testing-anti-patterns-zh-*.md\")\n\n\tinstance, err = b.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build plan prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn commandMethod(\"plan\"), instance, nil\n}\n```\n\nNew BuildPlan:\n```go\nfunc (p *PIBuilder) BuildPlan(requirement string, params map[string]string) (method string, instance string, err error) {\n\tif requirement == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"requirement cannot be empty\")\n\t}\n\n\trickDir := getParam(params, \"rick_dir\")\n\tjobPlanDir := getParam(params, \"job_plan_dir\")\n\tif jobPlanDir == \"\" {\n\t\tjobPlanDir = filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", \"job_N\", \"plan\")\n\t}\n\n\ttmpl, err := p.manager().LoadTemplate(\"plan\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load plan template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// 单文件内聚：关键 skill 内容内联进主产物（而非散落路径引用）。\n\t// 缺内联源时返回 error（非 panic / 非静默空内容）。\n\tinlineSkills, err := renderInlineSkills([]string{\"grilling\", \"tdd-zh\", \"testing-anti-patterns-zh\"})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to inline plan skills: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tb := prompt.NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"loops_context\", prompt.LoadLoopsContext(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"loops\")))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"domain_dir\", filepath.Join(rickDir, \"domain\"))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"user_requirement\", requirement)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"job_plan_dir\", jobPlanDir)\n\tb.SetVariable(\"rick_bin_path\", resolveRickBinPath())\n\tb.SetVariable(\"job_id\", extractJobID(jobPlanDir))\n\tb.SetVariable(\"grilling_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-prompts/skill_grilling.md\")\n\tb.SetVariable(\"tdd_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-tdd-zh-*.md\")\n\tb.SetVariable(\"testing_anti_patterns_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-testing-anti-patterns-zh-*.md\")\n\n\tinstance, err = b.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build plan prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// 内联段追加在主产物末尾，作为 pi 可识别的结构化「skill 内联段」。\n\tinstance += \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\\n\" + inlineSkills\n\treturn commandMethod(\"plan\"), instance, nil\n}\n```\n\nWait — I need to think about where the inline section goes. The plan.md template ends with the 9-step SOP. Appending after it is fine. But actually, the grilling content should ideally be near the SOP step 4 reference. But appending at the end is simpler and the test just greps for content. However, for \"pi 可识别的结构化引用\", a clearly-marked section is good.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — the \"内联段\" should be structured so pi recognizes it. I'll make the section header clear.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the `instance` already ends with `---\\n\\n` possibly? Let me check the plan.md template end. The plan.md ends with:\n\n```\n9. **输出**：按 task.md 格式保存到 `{{job_plan_dir}}/task{N}.md`\n```\n\nNo trailing `---`. So appending `\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\\n` is clean.\n\nNow, the `renderInlineSkills` produces sections like:\n```\n### skill:grilling\n\n<content>\n\n### skill:tdd-zh\n\n<content>\n\n### skill:testing-anti-patterns-zh\n\n<content>\n```\n\nWait, I have a leading `\\n` before `### skill:`. Let me adjust to avoid double newlines. Let me make the format clean:\n\n```go\nfunc renderInlineSkills(skills []string) (string, error) {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor i, name := range skills {\n\t\tcontent, err := prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif i > 0 {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"### skill:\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(name)\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stripYAMLFrontmatter(content))\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String(), nil\n}\n```\n\nThen in BuildPlan:\n```go\ninstance += \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\\n\\n\" + inlineSkills\n```\n\nThat's clean.\n\nNow for the doing_loop changes. `renderDoingLoop` now returns `(string, error)`. I need to update all 4 callers:\n1. `BuildDoing` (line ~297): `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(...))`.\n2. `BuildEasy` (line ~339): `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(...))`.\n3. `SaveDoingPrompt` (line ~479): `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(...))`.\n4. `SaveEasyPrompt` (line ~548): `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(...))`.\n\nLet me find all occurrences precisely.\n\nFrom the earlier grep of pibuilder.go:\n- line 297: `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"domain\"), \"<doing-prompts>/skill_debug_skill.md\"))` (BuildDoing)\n- line 339: `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(domainDir, filepath.Join(promptsDir, \"skill_debug_skill.md\")))` (BuildEasy)\n- line 479: `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"domain\"), debugSkillFile))` (SaveDoingPrompt)\n- line 548: `b.SetVariable(\"doing_loop_content\", renderDoingLoop(domainDir, debugSkillFile))` (SaveEasyPrompt)\n\nI need to change each to:\n```go\ndoingLoopContent, err := renderDoingLoop(...)\nif err != nil {\n    return \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to inline doing loop: %w\", err)  // or appropriate return\n}\nb.SetVariable(\"doin