{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dry-run works:\n- 542 lines (>0)\n- `{{` count 0\n- Grilling count 3 (≥1)\n\nNote there's a warning \"warn: LoadLoopsContext: no trigger in README.md, skipping\" which is a pre-existing behavior (LoadLoopsContext reads all .md files in loops dir including README.md). This is not related to my task, and it goes to stderr (log), not stdout. The `grep -c` counts stdout only. Good.\n\nWait, let me verify the warning is on stderr not stdout. The task10.py test uses `subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True, text=True)` and captures `p.stdout` and `p.stderr` separately. The log warning goes to stderr (log.Printf defaults to stderr). So `out` (stdout) is clean. The test passed, so this is fine.\n\nNow let me look at the dry-run output structure to make sure the inline section is well-formed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_44jLoevdWkypkZfazEmg8886","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && ./bin/rick plan --dry-run 2>/dev/null | tail -60"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":127,"output":288,"cacheRead":139904,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":212,"totalTokens":140319,"cost":{"input":0.000055245000000000004,"output":0.00025056,"cacheRead":0.0005071520000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000812957}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914256787,"responseId":"8b1784e9-7f93-4144-8a83-b43f12d533c8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
