"toolCallId":"call_00_ET_PDzTEskjDC9d3Y8xqymx5998","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Description: rick-gates 门禁 helper — 确定性 doing 门禁校验。\n\n\"\"\"rick-gates 门禁 helper — 确定性 doing 门禁校验。\n\nrick 侧确定性脚本（非 pi extension hook，hook 仅作通知/记录）。runtime.Run 在解析到\nagent_settled（pi 会话结束）后直接调用本脚本校验 doing 门禁，exit 非 0 = 门禁失败。\n\n校验语义（与原 doing_check 三项语义对齐）：\n1. tasks.json 可解析 —— doing/tasks.json 是合法 JSON 且含 tasks 数组。\n2. zombie 检测 —— 无遗留 running 状态任务。\n3. commit_hash 存在 —— status=success 的任务必须有非空 commit_hash。\n\n用法：python3 helper.py <doing_dir>\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n\ndef main(argv):\n    if len(argv) < 2:\n        print(\"usage: helper.py <doing_dir>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    doing_dir = argv[1]\n    tasks_json_path = os.path.join(doing_dir, \"tasks.json\")\n\n    # 1. tasks.json 可解析\n    try:\n        with open(tasks_json_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - 门禁错误串需兼容任意解析失败\n        print(\"tasks.json 不可解析: %s\" % e, file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    tasks = data.get(\"tasks\")\n    if not isinstance(tasks, list):\n        print(\"tasks.json 缺少 tasks 数组\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    for task in tasks:\n        task_id = task.get(\"task_id\", \"?\")\n        status = task.get(\"status\", \"\")\n\n        # 2. zombie 检测\n        if status == \"running\":\n            print(\"zombie running: task %s 仍处于 running 状态\" % task_id, file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n        # 3. commit_hash 存在\n        if status == \"success\":\n            commit_hash = task.get(\"commit_hash\", \"\")\n            if not commit_hash:\n                print(\"missing commit_hash: task %s 状态为 success 但 commit_hash 为空\" % task_id, file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n    print(\"gate passed\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913949503},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_ET_qWwfWyipWV8t9pXkCa5g1572","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Skills 目录规范\n\nSkill 是一个原子级能力单元（静态上下文），agent 在遇到触发条件时按需加载并执行一次。\n\n## 目录结构\n\n每个 skill 必须以**目录**形式存在：\n\n```\n.rick/skills/\n├── {name}_skill/\n│   ├── skill.md        # 必须：触发场景 / 预期效果 / 核心内容\n│   ├── helper.py       # 可选：Python 辅助脚本\n│   └── ...             # 可选：其他支撑文件\n└── deprecated/         # 已淘汰（连续3次dream未被引用）\n```\n\n**命名规则**：目录名以 `_skill` 结尾，如 `mark_task_success_skill/`。\n\n## 当前 Skills 索引\n\n| Skill | 触发场景 |\n|-------|---------|\n| test_script_practices_skill | 编写/调试 .rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tests/taskN.py |\n| zero_retry_task_design_skill | plan 阶段分解任务，降低 doing 重试率 |\n| dag_task_decomposition_skill | 设计复杂 task DAG，识别并行化机会 |\n| check_mechanism_skill | learning_check/dream_check 失败，理解修复方法 |\n| failure_feedback_skill | 理解/调整 doing 重试时失败信息传递机制 |\n| mark_task_success_skill | rick-gates 门禁报 missing commit_hash 时修复 |\n| global_ref_sync_skill | 修改核心名称/变量前先全局 grep 找引用 |\n| verify_go_changes_skill | 修改 Go 源文件后验证编译+测试通过 |\n| template_injection_skill | 向 plan/easy 模板注入新 skill 或修改变量 |\n\n## skill.md 格式（三段式）\n\n```markdown\n# skill:{name}（描述）\n\n## 触发场景\n什么情况下使用，要具体（\"当X时\" 不是 \"调试时\"）\n\n## 预期效果\n可量化的结果（\"减少重试次数\" 不够，要 \"一次运行通过\"）\n\n## 核心内容\n可直接执行的步骤/命令/决策树，含具体示例\n```\n\n## 淘汰标准\n\n连续 3 次 dream 未被引用的 skill → 移至 `deprecated/`。\n=== skills list files ===\nmock_agent_testing.py\nskill.md\n---\n# skill:verify-go-changes（验证 Go 代码修改）\n\n## 触发场景\n\n修改了 Go 源文件后，需要验证编译通过、单元测试和集成测试通过时使用。\n\n## 预期效果\n\n- 编译无报错\n- 单元测试全绿（精确匹配改动包，不跑全量）\n- 集成测试通过\n- dry-run 输出包含正确注入内容\n\n## 核心内容\n\n### Step 1：编译检查\n\n```bash\ngo build ./...\n# 或使用辅助脚本：\npython3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/build_rick.py\n```\n\n### Step 2：单元测试（精确范围，禁止 ./internal/...）\n\n```bash\n# 只跑改动的包，避免混入依赖真实 API key 的无关测试\ngo test ./internal/prompt/... -v\ngo test ./internal/executor/... -v\ngo test ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s -v\n```\n\n**禁止**：`go test ./internal/...` 全量，会混入依赖真实环境的无关测试。\n\n### Step 3：集成测试（如有）\n\n```bash\nbash tests/tools_integration_test.sh\n```\n\n### Step 4：dry-run 验证注入效果\n\n```bash\n./bin/rick doing job_N --dry-run | grep \"关键词\"\n./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep -c '{{未替换变量}}'  # 应为 0\n```\n\n### Go test 超时问题\n\n如果测试卡住 > 30s（卡在 retry sleep），检查是否有全局 `~/.rick/config.json` 设置了高 `max_retries`：\n\n```go\n// 在测试函数开头添加：\ndir := t.TempDir()\nt.Setenv(\"HOME\", dir)\n_ = os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(dir, \".rick\"), 0755)\n_ = os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, \".rick\", \"config.json\"), []byte(`{\"max_retries\":2}`), 0644)\n```\n\n### DIP 验证命令\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913949503},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the gate. The doing_check command is `rick tools doing_check job_35` but actually I see the tools.go only registers init-pi, theme, learning_check, dream_check. Let me check where doing_check is registered. The task prompt says \"第二步：格式检查 `rick tools doing_check job_35`\".\n\nWait, looking at the git log, there was \"task8: 做薄 cutover — 下沉 doing 调度与门禁到 pi，删除全部冗余 Go 包\". The tools.go doesn't show doing_check. Let me search for it more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_3OIFsqPMgvb4lvNbyjcd0595","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"doing_check\\|DoingCheck\\|doingCheck\" . --include=\"*.go\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"_test.go\" | head -30"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_1z0nDfdx6EPMKjxGHjrA3379","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && ./bin/rick tools --help 2>&1 | head -40; echo \"=== doing_check ===\"; ./bin/rick tools doing_check job_35 2>&1 | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1569,"output":308,"cacheRead":85120,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":124,"totalTokens":86997,"cost":{"input":0.0006825150000000001,"output":0.00026796000000000003,"cacheRead":0.00030856000000000004,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0012590350000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913949504,"responseId":"30ba087c-a36b-4f3d-86aa-593894e38530","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_3OIFsqPMgvb4lvNbyjcd0595","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913954609},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_1z0nDfdx6EPMKjxGHjrA3379","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"rick tools provides a set of validation and management commands for Rick workflows.\n\nThese commands are primarily used by AI agents during the learning phase.\nAn AI agent reads 'rick tools --help' to discover all available tools,\nthen decides which commands to invoke to complete its work.\n\nAvailable subcommands:\n  init-pi         Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + subagent extension\n  learning_check  Validate the learning directory structure for a job (incl. loops/skills format)\n  dream_check     Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/ (incl. loops/skills format)\n\nUsage:\n  rick tools [flags]\n  rick tools [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  dream_check    Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/\n  init-pi        Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + extensions + theme\n  learning_check Validate the learning directory structure for a job\n  theme          List or switch the pi TUI theme\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for tools\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --dry-run      Run in dry-run mode without making changes\n      --job string   Specify job ID (e.g., job_1)\n  -v, --verbose      Enable verbose output\n\nUse \"rick tools [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n=== doing_check ===\nrick tools provides a set of validation and management commands for Rick workflows.\n\nThese commands are primarily used by AI agents during the learning phase.\nAn AI agent reads 'rick tools --help' to discover all available tools,\nthen decides which commands to invoke to complete its work.\n\nAvailable subcommands:\n  init-pi         Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + subagent extension\n  learning_check  Validate the learning directory structure for a job (incl. loops/skills format)\n  dream_check     Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/ (incl. loops/skills format)\n\nUsage:\n  rick tools [flags]\n  rick tools [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  dream_check    Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/\n  init-pi        Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + extensions + theme\n  learning_check Validate the learning directory structure for a job\n  theme          List or switch the pi TUI theme\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913954609},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `doing_check` command doesn't exist anymore (task8 removed it, replaced by the rick-gates helper.py). The task prompt's \"第二步：格式检查\" says to run `rick tools doing_check job_35`, but that command no longer exists. Instead, the gate is now `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doing_dir>`.\n\nWait, but the task prompt I was given at the top says:\n\"## 第二步：格式检查\n`/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`\ncheck pass 后才算完成。\"\n\nThis seems to be an outdated prompt template. The doing_check was removed in task8. The current gate is `rick-gates/helper.py`.\n\nActually, let me check the git log and the deprecated loops. The doing gate is now the helper.py script. Let me verify what \"check pass\" means now. Actually, since the task8 already completed and removed doing_check, the actual gate is the rick-gates helper.py which I should run.\n\nLet me also check: there's a `mark_task_success_skill` which mentions the rick-gates gate. And the loop file `.rick/loops/tdd-red-green-refactor-loop.md` was modified (unstaged). Let me not worry about that.\n\nActually, the important thing: the doing gate now = `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doing_dir>`. The doing_dir = `.rick/jobs/job_35/doing`. I'll run that at the end to verify (task10 is \"running\" so it would fail with \"zombie running\" until I mark it success).\n\nLet me now focus on the actual implementation.\n\nLet me understand the full picture and design:\n\n**Goal**: Make `BuildPlan` (and BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop) inline key skill/loop content into the single .md product.\n\n**Key requirements**:\n1. `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name string) (string, error)` in prompt package (exported, wraps skillsFS.ReadFile, returns error on missing).\n2. `BuildPlan` must call `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` and inline its content; if missing → return error containing \"grilling\".\n3. `plan --dry-run` output must contain \"Grilling\" or \"结构化追问\" (grilling content inline).\n4. No unreplaced `{{` in dry-run output.\n\nLet me trace exactly what the plan template produces and where to inline grilling.\n\nCurrently in `BuildPlan`:\n```go\nb.SetVariable(\"grilling_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-prompts/skill_grilling.md\")\nb.SetVariable(\"tdd_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-tdd-zh-*.md\")\nb.SetVariable(\"testing_anti_patterns_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-testing-anti-patterns-zh-*.md\")\n```\n\nThe plan.md template references:\n- `{{grilling_skill_path}}` (in step 4)\n- `{{tdd_skill_path}}` (in 测试用例设计规范 + subagent_5)\n- `{{testing_anti_patterns_path}}` (in 测试用例设计规范 + subagent_5)\n\nThe test only checks grilling. But the KR says \"关键 skill/loop 内容内联\". Let me determine which skills are \"关键\" for each command.\n\nFor plan: grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh (these are the \"关键 skill\" referenced in the plan SOP).\n\nActually, let me think about the scope carefully. The task says \"本 task 只做结构内聚（产出形态），不改模板触发语言内容（task11）\". So I shouldn't rewrite the SOP text. I should keep the template structure but inline content.\n\nThe cleanest approach: Instead of setting `grilling_skill_path` to a file path, inline the grilling skill content directly. But the template text says \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\". If I replace `{{grilling_skill_path}}` with the full content, the template would read \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：<full content>）\" which is awkward.\n\nBetter approach: Add a new section in the template that inlines the skill content, OR change the variable semantics.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The KR3 says \"单文件含 pi 可识别的结构化引用（agent frontmatter / skill 内联段）\". So the single file should have \"skill 内联段\" (skill inline sections).\n\nLet me design the plan template to have a skill inline section. But the task says \"不改模板触发语言内容\". Hmm, but \"结构内聚（产出形态）\" IS the task, so adding an inline section is allowed; just don't change the trigger language (the SOP steps wording).\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. \"不改模板触发语言内容（task11）\" — task11 is \"把自然语言 subagent 触发词等价迁移为 pi 显式触发语法\". So task10 must NOT touch the trigger language (e.g. \"I will use skill:tdd\", \"加载 skill:grilling\", subagent trigger words). But task10 CAN add inline content sections.\n\nLet me look at what would be the minimal, clean change:\n\nOption A: Inline the grilling/tdd/testing-anti-patterns content into the plan.md template via a new variable `{{skill_inline_sections}}` that contains the full skill content appended at the end (or in a dedicated section). And keep the path references as-is (or remove them).\n\nBut the test requires grilling content inline AND the KR says \"散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\". So I should inline content AND reduce path references.\n\nHmm, but there's a tension: if I keep \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\" AND inline the content, then there's redundancy but it's fine — the path reference is still there for the pi skills mechanism, but the content is also inlined.\n\nActually, let me re-read the KR1 note once more, very carefully:\n\n\"内聚实现 = 运行时经 prompt 包的导出函数 `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)`（封装 `skillsFS.ReadFile`）读取（缺失返回 error），而非硬编码 Go 常量——builder 是独立包、`skillsFS` 未导出，必须经导出函数跨包访问；内聚范围 = 模板/skill 内容，job 级动态内容（task.md/debug/OKR）仍按 task5 走路径注入，pi 自行 read；「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\"\n\nOK so this note is quite dense. Let me parse each clause:\n\n1. \"内聚实现 = 运行时经 prompt 包的导出函数 `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)`（封装 `skillsFS.ReadFile`）读取（缺失返回 error），而非硬编码 Go 常量\" — Implementation: use `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)` (wraps skillsFS.ReadFile, returns error on missing), NOT hardcoded Go constants.\n\n2. \"builder 是独立包、`skillsFS` 未导出，必须经导出函数跨包访问\" — builder is a separate package, skillsFS is unexported, must access via exported function.\n\n3. \"内聚范围 = 模板/skill 内容，job 级动态内容（task.md/debug/OKR）仍按 task5 走路径注入，pi 自行 read\" — Cohesion scope = template/skill content; job-level dynamic content (task.md/debug/OKR) still path-injected per task5, pi reads them itself.\n\n4. \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\" — \"Single-file cohesion\" means method (system prompt) is self-contained (key loop/skill content inlined into method); on-demand skills (grilling/tdd) still go through pi skills mechanism (task5); the two don't conflict.\n\nOK so point 4 is the key nuance: \"单文件内聚\" = the METHOD (system prompt) is self-contained. The \"关键 loop/skill\" content is inlined into method. But grilling/tdd are \"执行期按需技能\" that still go through pi skills mechanism.\n\nWait, but this directly conflicts with the test which requires grilling content inline in `plan --dry-run` (instance).\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. Let me re-read the test boundary case once more:\n\n\"边界（单文件内聚）：前置条件 = build 成功；输入 = `plan --dry-run`；操作 = `./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep -cE 'Grilling|结构化追问'`；预期 = ≥1（grilling skill 内容内联进主产物，而非仅 `skill_grilling.md` 路径引用）。\"\n\nThe comment says \"grilling skill 内容内联进主产物\" (grilling skill content inlined into main product).\n\nSo the test is clear: grilling content inlined into the main product (plan dry-run output).\n\nI think the resolution is:\n- The KR note point 4 is describing the ARCHITECTURE: method is self-contained (key loops/skills inlined), while grilling/tdd go through pi skills. BUT, the \"主产物\" (main product) = the single .md file = which is BOTH method + instance? Or just instance?\n\nActually, let me reconsider what \"主产物\" (main product) means in the context of the builder. Looking at the code comments:\n\nIn pibuilder.go:\n```\n// PIBuilder is the pi 统一入口 ... produces two artifacts per command:\n//\tmethod   — command-specific method layer ... injected into pi's system prompt via --append-system-prompt.\n//\tinstance — job context / paths, injected as the user prompt file.\n```\n\nSo there are TWO artifacts: method + instance. The \"主产物\" (main product) in the test = the dry-run output = instance (for plan).\n\nBut the KR1 note says \"单文件内聚\" = method self-contained.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I'm overcomplicating. Let me re-read the task goal:\n\n\"每个 cmd 的 pibuilder 产物把 skill/loop 内容内联进单个 .md 产物（而非散落文件 + 路径引用），可被 pi 直接加载执行。\"\n\n\"每个 cmd 的 pibuilder 产物\" = each cmd's pibuilder product. \"把 skill/loop 内容内联进单个 .md 产物\" = inline skill/loop content into a single .md product.\n\nSo the \"单个 .md 产物\" is the single file that pi loads directly. For the pi loading, the file that pi reads is the instance file (plan_prompt.md). The method goes via --append-system-prompt.\n\nSo the \"主产物\" = the instance file (plan_prompt.md), and the grilling content should be inlined there.\n\nNow the KR1 note \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含\" — I think this is a slightly imprecise/confusing note, but the KEY actionable requirement is clear from the test: inline grilling content into the plan instance, and use ReadEmbeddedSkill.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the intended design is:\n- method (system prompt) = self-contained, inlines key loop/skill content.\n- instance (user prompt) = the \"单文件\" that ALSO inlines the command's on-demand skill content (grilling/tdd) so pi doesn't need scattered files.\n\nActually, re-reading point 4 one more time: \"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\".\n\nI think this is saying: The \"单文件内聚\" concept (from spec KR3.1) specifically refers to the method being self-contained. The on-demand skills (grilling/tdd) still go through pi skills. So there's NO conflict between \"单文件内聚\" and \"pi skills mechanism\".\n\nBut the test clearly requires grilling content inline in the plan dry-run output. So maybe the interpretation is:\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider what grilling is for the plan command. In the plan SOP, step 4 is \"grilling 追问：加载 skill:grilling\". This is a KEY part of the plan method. So grilling IS a \"关键 skill\" for plan (it's part of the plan SOP), not just an \"执行期按需技能\".\n\nHmm, but point 4 explicitly lists \"grilling/tdd 等\" as \"执行期按需技能\".\n\nOK, I'm going in circles. Let me just focus on making the test pass while being faithful to the clear, actionable parts:\n\n1. Add `ReadEmbeddedSkill(name)` to prompt package. ✅ (clear requirement)\n2. `BuildPlan` uses `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` and inlines content; error propagates if missing. ✅ (clear from test 3)\n3. `plan --dry-run` output contains grilling content. ✅ (clear from test 2)\n\nFor the \"method 自包含\" part, I'll also inline key loop/skill content into the method where appropriate (e.g., doing_loop into doing method), but the primary visible change is the instance inlining.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the relationship more holistically. Let me re-read the KR1 first sentence:\n\n\"pibuilder 的 BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop 产出的主产物把关键 skill/loop 内容内联（内聚单文件），散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\"\n\nSo: \"BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop 产出的主产物\" (the main product of these methods) \"把关键 skill/loop 内容内联\" (inlines key skill/loop content). \"散落 skill 文件引用下降\" (scattered skill file references decrease).\n\nSo the \"主产物\" for each of these 4 methods should inline key skill/loop content.\n\nFor BuildPlan: 主产物 = instance (plan_prompt.md). Key skills = grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh.\nFor BuildDoing: 主产物 = instance (doing_prompt.md). Key loop = doing_loop (already inlined). Key skill = debug_skill.\nFor BuildEasy: 主产物 = instance (easy_prompt.md). Key skills = grilling, debug_skill, learning_loop, etc.\nFor BuildHumanLoop: 主产物 = instance (sense_loop prompt). Key skills = sense/think/research/exporter (already inlined via GenerateHumanLoopPrompt?).\n\nOK so I think the actual scope is: inline the key skill content into the INSTANCE (main product), using ReadEmbeddedSkill.\n\nNow, let me figure out the exact mechanics. The template variables that currently hold file PATHS:\n- plan.md: `grilling_skill_path`, `tdd_skill_path`, `testing_anti_patterns_path`\n- doing.md: `doing_loop_content` (already inlined content), `grilling_section` (built by buildGrillingSection which uses a path), `session_wrap_section` (uses learning_loop path), `import_ctx_content` (already inlined content).\n\nLet me focus on the MINIMUM to satisfy the test + KR, while keeping changes clean.\n\n**Minimal plan for BuildPlan:**\n1. Read grilling content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")`. If error → return error (wrapped with \"grilling\").\n2. Read tdd-zh content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"tdd-zh\")`. If error → return error? Or maybe not required. The KR says \"缺失返回 error\". The test only checks grilling. But for robustness, I'll read all key skills and error on missing.\n3. Read testing-anti-patterns-zh content via `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"testing-anti-patterns-zh\")`.\n4. Inline these contents into the instance. I'll add a new section/variable in the plan template, e.g. `{{skill_inline_sections}}`, that contains the full skill content.\n\nWait, but \"不改模板触发语言内容\". Adding a variable `{{skill_inline_sections}}` to the plan template is a structural change (产出形态), which is this task's job. It's not changing \"触发语言\" (trigger language). So it's fine.\n\nLet me design the template changes:\n\nFor plan.md, I'll add a section near the end (or before the SOP) that inlines the skills:\n\nActually, let me think about where the inline content should go. The test greps for \"Grilling|结构化追问\" in the plan --dry-run output. As long as the grilling content (which contains \"Grilling（结构化追问协议）\" etc.) is in the output, the test passes.\n\nThe cleanest design: append a \"## 内联 Skill/Loop 内容\" section at the end of the plan prompt that contains the full content of grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh.\n\nBut wait, that would duplicate content if the SOP still references paths. Actually the KR says \"散落 skill 文件引用下降（关键 skill 内联而非仅路径）\", meaning I should REDUCE the path references by inlining.\n\nHmm, but the SOP text \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\" is \"触发语言\" that task11 will migrate. So I shouldn't touch it.\n\nLet me think about the cleanest approach that:\n1. Inlines grilling content (so test passes).\n2. Uses ReadEmbeddedSkill.\n3. Reduces path references (replaces `grilling_skill_path` placeholder with inlined content, or removes the path variable).\n\nActually, maybe the simplest and most faithful approach:\n\nThe `grilling_skill_path` variable currently holds a path placeholder. Instead, I change the semantics: the template's \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\" gets its path REPLACED by... no wait.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe I should:\n1. Change the plan.md template to have a dedicated \"skill 内联段\" section, e.g.:\n\n```\n## 内联技能内容（单文件内聚）\n\n### skill:grilling\n\n{{grilling_content}}\n\n### skill:tdd\n\n{{tdd_content}}\n\n### skill:testing-anti-patterns\n\n{{testing_anti_patterns_content}}\n```\n\nAnd keep the SOP step 4 \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：X）\" as-is (or change the path to point to the inline section).\n\nActually, hmm. Let me check if the SOP references need to change. The task says \"不改模板触发语言内容（task11）\". So I keep \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\" as the trigger language, but I inline the content so pi can find it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing from the perspective of \"what does pi actually need\". The goal is: pi should be able to load the single .md file and have everything it needs (no scattered skill files).\n\nCurrently:\n- plan_prompt.md references skill_grilling.md by path → pi reads that separate file.\n\nAfter:\n- plan_prompt.md contains grilling content inline → pi reads only plan_prompt.md.\n\nSo the inline content REPLACES the need for the separate file. The SOP step can stay as \"加载 skill:grilling\" but the content is inline.\n\nFor the template, I think the cleanest is:\n- Keep the SOP step 4 text \"加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`）\" but change `grilling_skill_path` to point to the inline section, OR just keep the path as a reference but ALSO inline the content.\n\nActually, let me look at how the existing doing_loop inlining works, since that's the existing pattern I should follow:\n\nIn doing.md:\n```\n{{loop_step_header}}\n\n{{doing_loop_content}}\n```\n\nAnd `doing_loop_content` = the full doing_loop skill content (stripped of frontmatter, with domain_dir and debug_skill_path substituted). So the doing_loop is FULLY inlined (its content replaces the path reference).\n\nSo for plan, the analogous approach: inline grilling content into the plan prompt via a `{{grilling_content}}` variable, and the SOP step 4 references it inline.\n\nLet me design the plan.md changes:\n\nCurrently:\n```\n4. **grilling 追问**：加载 skill:grilling（路径：`{{grilling_skill_path}}`），对用户需求逐问追问...\n```\n\nAnd:\n```\n设计 `# 测试方法` 章节时，必须参考：\n- skill:tdd（路径：`{{tdd_skill_path}}`）— ...\n- skill:testing-anti-patterns（路径：`{{testing_anti_patterns_path}}`）— ...\n```\n\nAnd:\n```\n- subagent_5：测试用例完整性 —— 参考 skill:tdd（`{{tdd_skill_path}}`）和 skill:testing-anti-patterns（`{{testing_anti_patterns_path}}`）...\n```\n\nThe cleanest: change these path references to inline the content directly. But that would make the SOP text awkward.\n\nAlternative: Add a dedicated inline section at the end of the template:\n\n```\n## 内联技能（单文件内聚）\n\n### skill:grilling\n\n{{grilling_content}}\n\n### skill:tdd\n\n{{tdd_content}}\n\n### skill:testing-anti-patterns\n\n{{testing_anti_patterns_content}}\n```\n\nAnd change the SOP references to point to \"上文内联的 skill:grilling 内容\" instead of a file path. But that changes trigger language.\n\nHmm. Actually, the task says \"不改模板触发语言内容\". Let me interpret this narrowly: don't change the WORDS that trigger subagent/skill behavior (like \"I will use skill:tdd\", \"加载 skill:grilling\", \"启动子 Agent\"). I CAN change the \"路径：X\" part to \"见下文内联内容\" because that's structural, not trigger language.\n\nActually, wait, let me reconsider even more carefully. Let me re-read the boundary test comment:\n\n\"grilling skill 内容内联进主产物，而非仅 `skill_grilling.md` 路径引用\"\n\nSo the concern is: currently the output only has a path reference (`skill_grilling.md`). After the change, the output should have the actual content. The test just greps for \"Grilling|结构化追问\" which is in the grilling content.\n\nSo the minimal change is: inline grilling content somewhere in the plan instance output.\n\nLet me now decide the exact implementation. I'll do a clean, comprehensive approach:\n\n**Prompt package changes (manager.go):**\n\nAdd:\n```go\n// ReadEmbeddedSkill reads a single embedded skill's content by name.\n// It wraps skillsFS.ReadFile so external packages (builder) can access\n// embedded skill content without the unexported skillsFS. Missing skill\n// returns an error (no silent empty content).\nfunc ReadEmbeddedSkill(name string) (string, error) {\n\tpath := skillPath(name)\n\tcontent, err := skillsFS.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"embedded skill %q not found: %w\", name, err)\n\t}\n\treturn string(content), nil\n}\n```\n\nWhere `skillPath(name)` is a helper that maps name → templates/skills/{name}.md. Actually, the existing `LoadCoreSkills` uses `path := \"templates/skills/\" + name + \".md\"`. But there's a special case: \"tdd/testing-anti-patterns\" maps to templates/skills/tdd/testing-anti-patterns.md. Let me check.\n\nLooking at LoadCoreSkills comment:\n```\n// Names like \"tdd/testing-anti-patterns\" map to templates/skills/tdd/testing-anti-patterns.md.\n// All other names map to templates/skills/{name}.md.\n```\n\nBut then the actual code just does `path := \"templates/skills/\" + name + \".md\"`. Wait, so \"tdd/testing-anti-patterns\" would map to \"templates/skills/tdd/testing-anti-patterns.md\"? No wait, \"templates/skills/\" + \"tdd/testing-anti-patterns\" + \".md\" = \"templates/skills/tdd/testing-anti-patterns.md\". Yes, that's correct because the name contains a slash.\n\nBut looking at the actual skill files, they are flat: `templates/skills/tdd-zh.md`, `templates/skills/testing-anti-patterns-zh.md`. So the names used are \"tdd-zh\" and \"testing-anti-patterns-zh\".\n\nLet me verify by listing the skills directory again:\n```\ntemplates/skills/debug_skill.md\ntemplates/skills/doing_loop.md\ntemplates/skills/evolve-skills.md\ntemplates/skills/exporter.md\ntemplates/skills/gen-domain.md\ntemplates/skills/gen-loop.md\ntemplates/skills/gen-skill.md\ntemplates/skills/grilling.md\ntemplates/skills/import_ctx.md\ntemplates/skills/learning_loop.md\ntemplates/skills/refactor-rfc.md\ntemplates/skills/research.md\ntemplates/skills/sense.md\ntemplates/skills/source-context-consistency.md\ntemplates/skills/tdd-zh.md\ntemplates/skills/testing-anti-patterns-zh.md\ntemplates/skills/testing.md\ntemplates/skills/think.md\ntemplates/skills/write_spec.md\n```\n\nSo the skill names used in code are: \"grilling\", \"tdd-zh\", \"testing-anti-patterns-zh\", \"debug_skill\", \"doing_loop\", \"gen-skill\", \"gen-loop\", \"gen-domain\", \"learning_loop\", \"import_ctx\".\n\nThe `WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_grilling.md\", \"grilling\")` writes skill name \"grilling\".\n\nSo `ReadEmbeddedSkill(\"grilling\")` should map to \"templates/skills/grilling.md\".\n\nLet me design the helper. The current `LoadCoreSkills` maps name → \"templates/skills/\" + name + \".md\". For consistency, I'll add a `skillPath(name)` helper used by both. Actually, let me keep it simple and just inline the path logic.\n\nActually, there might be a subtlety. Let me check the `WriteSkillFileWithVars` and how `learning_loop` is loaded. It uses `LoadCoreSkills([]string{\"learning_loop\"})` → \"templates/skills/learning_loop.md\". Good.\n\nNow let me think about the builder changes.\n\n**Builder changes (pibuilder.go):**\n\nFor `BuildPlan`:\n1. Read grilling, tdd-zh, testing-anti-patterns-zh contents via `prompt.ReadEmbeddedSkill`.\n2. Inline them into the instance via a new template variable.\n\nFor `BuildDoing` and `BuildEasy`:\n1. The doing_loop is already inlined via `renderDoingLoop` → but that uses `prompt.LoadCoreSkills` (which logs warning and skips, no error). Should I switch to `ReadEmbeddedSkill` for doing_loop too? The KR says \"关键 loop/skill 内容内联\" and \"内聚实现 = ReadEmbeddedSkill\". So yes, I should switch doing_loop to ReadEmbeddedSkill and propagate errors.\n\nFor `BuildHumanLoop`:\n1. It delegates to `prompt.GenerateHumanLoopPrompt` / `GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile`. These already inline sense/think/research/exporter templates (they're templates, not skills). Let me check human_loop_prompt.go.\n\nLet me read human_loop_prompt.go and the other prompt files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ScabR7ybz1lfe7Sk9akf1972","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/prompt/human_loop_prompt.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_ZcQJ5Kx68XwOtF4MnONf9490","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/prompt/dream_prompt.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_6cGYkALkzC3UYREbIfcq4583","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/prompt/ctrl_prompt.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":602,"output":6374,"cacheRead":86912,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6205,"totalTokens":93888,"cost":{"input":0.00026187,"output":0.00554538,"cacheRead":0.00031505600000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.006122306}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913954610,"responseId":"41855d2a-588c-468c-ba39-1306b605b0be","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ScabR7ybz1lfe7Sk9akf1972","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package prompt\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n)\n\n// GenerateHumanLoopPrompt generates the human-loop prompt string (for dry-run).\n// Returns the main sense_loop prompt content.\nfunc GenerateHumanLoopPrompt(topic string, rfcDir string, draftDir string, manager *PromptManager) (string, error) {\n\tif manager == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"prompt manager cannot be nil\")\n\t}\n\n\tmainTmpl, err := manager.LoadTemplate(\"sense_loop\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load sense_loop template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tbuilder := NewPromptBuilder(mainTmpl)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"topic\", topic)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"rfc_dir\", rfcDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"draft_dir\", draftDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loop_dir\", \"<draft>/loops/loop_N\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"think_agent_path\", \"<draft>/loops/loop_N/prompts/think.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"research_agent_path\", \"<draft>/loops/loop_N/prompts/research.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"exporter_agent_path\", \"<draft>/loops/loop_N/prompts/exporter.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"max_retries\", \"5\")\n\n\tcontent, err := builder.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build sense_loop prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn content, nil\n}\n\n// GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile generates the human-loop prompt and saves all files to\n// loopDir/prompts/ for persistence across sessions.\n// Returns mainFile (sense_loop), thinkFile, researchFile, exporterFile, and any error.\nfunc GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile(topic string, rfcDir string, draftDir string, loopDir string, manager *PromptManager) (string, string, string, string, error) {\n\tif manager == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"prompt manager cannot be nil\")\n\t}\n\n\tpromptsDir := loopDir + \"/prompts\"\n\tbriefsDir := loopDir + \"/briefs\"\n\n\tfor _, d := range []string{promptsDir, briefsDir} {\n\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(d, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create directory %s: %w\", d, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Write all skill files (sense/think/research/exporter)\n\tsenseSkillFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_sense.md\", \"sense\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write sense skill: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tthinkSkillFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_think.md\", \"think\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write think skill: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tresearchSkillFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_research.md\", \"research\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write research skill: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\texporterSkillFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_exporter.md\", \"exporter\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write exporter skill: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Build and save think subagent prompt\n\tthinkTmpl, err := manager.LoadTemplate(\"think\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load think template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tthinkBuilder := NewPromptBuilder(thinkTmpl)\n\tthinkBuilder.SetVariable(\"draft_dir\", draftDir)\n\tthinkBuilder.SetVariable(\"rfc_dir\", rfcDir)\n\tthinkBuilder.SetVariable(\"loop_dir\", loopDir)\n\tthinkBuilder.SetVariable(\"think_skill_path\", thinkSkillFile)\n\tthinkFile, err := thinkBuilder.BuildAndSaveToDir(\"think\", promptsDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save think: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Build and save research subagent prompt\n\tresearchTmpl, err := manager.LoadTemplate(\"research\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load research template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tresearchBuilder := NewPromptBuilder(researchTmpl)\n\tresearchBuilder.SetVariable(\"draft_dir\", draftDir)\n\tresearchBuilder.SetVariable(\"rfc_dir\", rfcDir)\n\tresearchBuilder.SetVariable(\"loop_dir\", loopDir)\n\tresearchBuilder.SetVariable(\"research_skill_path\", researchSkillFile)\n\tresearchFile, err := researchBuilder.BuildAndSaveToDir(\"research\", promptsDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save research: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Build and save exporter subagent prompt\n\texporterTmpl, err := manager.LoadTemplate(\"exporter\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load exporter template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\texporterBuilder := NewPromptBuilder(exporterTmpl)\n\texporterBuilder.SetVariable(\"draft_dir\", draftDir)\n\texporterBuilder.SetVariable(\"rfc_dir\", rfcDir)\n\texporterBuilder.SetVariable(\"loop_dir\", loopDir)\n\texporterBuilder.SetVariable(\"exporter_skill_path\", exporterSkillFile)\n\texporterFile, err := exporterBuilder.BuildAndSaveToDir(\"exporter\", promptsDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save exporter: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Build and save main sense_loop prompt\n\tmainTmpl, err := manager.LoadTemplate(\"sense_loop\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load sense_loop template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tbuilder := NewPromptBuilder(mainTmpl)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"topic\", topic)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"rfc_dir\", rfcDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"draft_dir\", draftDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loop_dir\", loopDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"think_agent_path\", thinkFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"research_agent_path\", researchFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"exporter_agent_path\", exporterFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"max_retries\", \"5\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"max_backflows\", \"3\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"min_assumptions\", \"5\")\n\n\tmainFile, err := builder.BuildAndSaveToDir(\"sense_loop\", promptsDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build and save sense_loop prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\t_ = senseSkillFile // sense skill written for subagent reference\n\n\treturn mainFile, thinkFile, researchFile, exporterFile, nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914021765},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_ZcQJ5Kx68XwOtF4MnONf9490","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package prompt\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// GenerateDreamPrompt generates the dream prompt content with placeholder paths (for dry-run).\nfunc GenerateDreamPrompt(jobIDs []string, rickDir string) (string, error) {\n\tmgr := NewPromptManager()\n\ttmpl, err := mgr.LoadTemplate(\"dream\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load dream template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tbuilder := NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"pending_jobs\", formatPendingJobs(jobIDs))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"run_logs\", loadRunLogs(rickDir))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loops_context\", LoadLoopsContext(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"loops\")))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loops_dir\", \"<loops_dir>\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"skills_dir\", \"<skills_dir>\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"domain_dir\", \"<domain_dir>\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"sense_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-dream-skill-sense-*.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"evolve_skills_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-dream-skill-evolve-skills-*.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_skill_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-dream-skill-gen-skill-*.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_loop_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-dream-skill-gen-loop-*.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_domain_path\", \"<tmp>/rick-dream-skill-gen-domain-*.md\")\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"rick_bin_path\", \"<rick>\")\n\tcontent, err := builder.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build dream prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tactPathContent := loadActPaths(jobIDs, rickDir)\n\tif actPathContent != \"\" {\n\t\tcontent += \"\\n\\n## 行为轨迹文件路径（按需读取）\\n\\n\" + actPathContent\n\t}\n\treturn content, nil\n}\n\n// GenerateDreamPromptFile generates the dream phase prompt and saves it to .rick/dream/prompts/.\n// jobIDs is the list of jobs to process; rickDir is the .rick directory path.\n// All files are persistent; no cleanup needed.\nfunc GenerateDreamPromptFile(jobIDs []string, rickDir string) (string, []string, error) {\n\tmgr := NewPromptManager()\n\n\ttmpl, err := mgr.LoadTemplate(\"dream\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load dream template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tdreamDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"dream\")\n\tpromptsDir, err := EnsurePromptsDir(dreamDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create dream prompts dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tsenseFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_sense.md\", \"sense\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, err\n\t}\n\tevolveFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_evolve_skills.md\", \"evolve-skills\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, err\n\t}\n\tgenSkillFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_gen_skill.md\", \"gen-skill\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, err\n\t}\n\tgenLoopFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_gen_loop.md\", \"gen-loop\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, err\n\t}\n\tgenDomainFile, err := WriteSkillFile(promptsDir, \"skill_gen_domain.md\", \"gen-domain\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, err\n\t}\n\n\tloopsDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"loops\")\n\tskillsDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\")\n\tdomainDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"domain\")\n\tbuilder := NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"pending_jobs\", formatPendingJobs(jobIDs))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"run_logs\", loadRunLogs(rickDir))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loops_context\", LoadLoopsContext(loopsDir))\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"loops_dir\", loopsDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"skills_dir\", skillsDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"domain_dir\", domainDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"sense_skill_path\", senseFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"evolve_skills_skill_path\", evolveFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_skill_path\", genSkillFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_loop_path\", genLoopFile)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"gen_domain_path\", genDomainFile)\n\tprojectRoot, _ := os.Getwd()\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"rick_bin_path\", filepath.Join(projectRoot, \"bin\", \"rick\"))\n\n\tcontent, err := builder.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build dream prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Append act-path context for each job\n\tactPathContent := loadActPaths(jobIDs, rickDir)\n\tif actPathContent != \"\" {\n\t\tcontent += \"\\n\\n## 行为轨迹文件路径（按需读取）\\n\\n\" + actPathContent\n\t}\n\n\tpromptFile := filepath.Join(promptsDir, \"dream_prompt.md\")\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(promptFile, []byte(content), 0644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write dream prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn promptFile, nil, nil\n}\n\n\nfunc formatPendingJobs(jobIDs []string) string {\n\tif len(jobIDs) == 0 {\n\t\treturn \"（无待处理 jobs）\"\n\t}\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor _, id := range jobIDs {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"- \" + id + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n\nfunc loadRunLogs(rickDir string) string {\n\tif rickDir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"（无历史 dream 记录）\"\n\t}\n\tdreamDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"dream\")\n\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dreamDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"（无历史 dream 记录）\"\n\t}\n\n\tvar logs []string\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tname := e.Name()\n\t\tif !e.IsDir() && strings.HasPrefix(name, \"dream_run_\") && strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_log.md\") {\n\t\t\tlogs = append(logs, name)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(logs) == 0 {\n\t\treturn \"（无历史 dream 记录）\"\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(logs)\n\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor _, name := range logs {\n\t\tcontent, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dreamDir, name))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"### \" + name + \"\\n\\n\")\n\t\tsb.Write(content)\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n\nfunc loadActPaths(jobIDs []string, rickDir string) string {\n\tif len(jobIDs) == 0 || rickDir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tfor _, jobID := range jobIDs {\n\t\tdoingTasksDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\", \"tasks\")\n\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(doingTasksDir)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\t\tif !e.IsDir() {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tactPath := filepath.Join(doingTasksDir, e.Name(), \"act-path.md\")\n\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(actPath); err == nil {\n\t\t\t\tsb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf(\"- `%s`\\n\", actPath))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914021765},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_6cGYkALkzC3UYREbIfcq4583","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package prompt\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n)\n\n// GenerateCtrlPromptFile generates the ctrl monitoring prompt for a given job.\n// The prompt is persisted to doing/prompts/ctrl_prompt.md and its path is returned.\nfunc GenerateCtrlPromptFile(jobID, rickDir string) (string, error) {\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\tplanDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"plan\")\n\ttasksJSONPath := filepath.Join(doingDir, \"tasks.json\")\n\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(doingDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"doing directory not found for job %s: %s\", jobID, doingDir)\n\t}\n\n\ttasksJSONContent := readFileOrDefault(tasksJSONPath, `{\"tasks\": []}`)\n\n\tpromptsDir, err := EnsurePromptsDir(doingDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create prompts dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tmgr := NewPromptManager()\n\ttmpl, err := mgr.LoadTemplate(\"ctrl\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load ctrl template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tbuilder := NewPromptBuilder(tmpl)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"job_id\", jobID)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"doing_dir\", doingDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"plan_dir\", planDir)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"tasks_json_path\", tasksJSONPath)\n\tbuilder.SetVariable(\"tasks_json_content\", tasksJSONContent)\n\n\tcontent, err := builder.Build()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build ctrl prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tpromptFile := filepath.Join(promptsDir, \"ctrl_prompt.md\")\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(promptFile, []byte(content), 0644); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write ctrl prompt: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn promptFile, nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914021765},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a full picture. Let me look at the remaining test files for builder and prompt to understand what might break, and check the existing tests that reference `grilling_skill_path` etc.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_09e0Q1ysVvPsgZfJKqSb7139","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"grilling_skill_path\\|tdd_skill_path\\|testing_anti_patterns_path\\|LoadCoreSkills\\|ReadEmbeddedSkill\\|grilling\" internal/ --include=\"*.go\" | grep -v \"_test.go\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_fGO7SxIAl49OvgohuxwY1877","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"grilling\\|Grilli