ance (plan_prompt.md), and grilling content should be inlined there. The \"method 自包含\" note is about the method ALSO being self-contained (which it already is, being a SOP string).\n\nActually, let me just re-read the KR1 note ONE more time and parse it as a parenthetical clarification rather than a hard requirement:\n\n\"「单文件内聚」指 method（system prompt）这一份自包含（关键 loop/skill 内容内联进 method），执行期按需技能（grilling/tdd 等）仍走 pi skills 机制（task5），二者不冲突\"\n\nParse: \"单文件内聚\" refers to [the fact that] method (system prompt) is self-contained (key loop/skill content inlined into method). On-demand skills (grilling/tdd etc.) still use pi skills mechanism. The two don't conflict.\n\nHmm wait, but then grilling is listed as an \"执行期按需技能\" that \"仍走 pi skills 机制\". So grilling should NOT be inlined?? But the test requires grilling inline!\n\nThere's a genuine contradiction between the KR note's parenthetical and the test. The test is the authoritative acceptance gate (task10.py). And the task10.md's own 测试方法 section 2 explicitly says \"grilling skill 内容内联进主产物\".\n\nSo I'll follow the test and the task10.md 测试方法 (which is more specific and authoritative than the KR note's parenthetical). The grilling content gets inlined into the plan instance.\n\nI think the KR note's parenthetical was written with a slightly different mental model (maybe thinking of \"method\" loosely as \"the main product\"). The key ACTIONABLE requirements are:\n1. Use `ReadEmbeddedSkill` (clear).\n2. Inline key skill/loop content into the main product (clear from 任务目标 + 测试方法).\n3. Error on missing skill (clear from 测试方法 3).\n\nLet me proceed with Option B, and ALSO make the method self-contained where it makes sense (for doing, inline doing_loop into method; but doing_loop is already inlined into instance via renderDoingLoop).\n\nActually, let me simplify and just do the clean, test-driven implementation:\n\n1. `ReadEmbeddedSkill` in prompt package (+ unit tests).\n2. `BuildPlan` inlines grilling/tdd-zh/testing-anti-patterns-zh into instance, errors on missing.\n3. `BuildDoing`/`BuildEasy`: switch `renderDoingLoop` to `ReadEmbeddedSkill` + propagate error (so doing_loop missing → error, consistent).\n4. `BuildEasy`: inline grilling content (via ReadEmbeddedSkill) — easy also has grilling as key skill.\n\nFor `BuildHumanLoop`: leave structure but maybe not needed. I'll do a light touch — actually, the human-loop's main prompt references think/research/exporter agent paths (not skills). Those are separate agent prompts (registered via env). The \"关键 skill\" for human-loop (sense/think/research/exporter) are written as skill files via `GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile`. I'll leave BuildHumanLoop as-is since it's a different structure and not tested. But I should at least ensure I don't break it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the scope to be safe. The KR1 says \"BuildPlan/BuildDoing/BuildEasy/BuildHumanLoop 产出的主产物把关键 skill/loop 内容内联\". Let me handle all four:\n\n- BuildPlan: inline grilling/tdd-zh/testing-anti-patterns-zh ✓\n- BuildDoing: doing_loop already inlined (via renderDoingLoop). Switch to ReadEmbeddedSkill. Also, debug_skill is referenced by path (in doing_loop's `{{debug_skill_path}}`). Should I inline debug_skill? The doing_loop references `{{debug_skill_path}}` which points to a written skill file. Inlining debug_skill would be the \"关键 skill\" for doing. Hmm. But debug_skill.md has `{{sense_skill_path}}` which needs substitution. This is getting complex.\n\nLet me be pragmatic: the doing_loop is the \"关键 loop\" for doing, and it's already inlined. I'll switch its loading to ReadEmbeddedSkill (error propagation). That's the main structural change for doing. I won't inline debug_skill (it's an execution-time on-demand skill referenced inside doing_loop's DEBUG step — exactly the \"执行期按需技能\" that should stay as pi skills per the KR note).\n\n- BuildEasy: doing_loop already inlined + grilling is the key skill for easy. I'll inline grilling. (grilling.md has 0 `{{`, safe.)\n\n- BuildHumanLoop: the sense_loop main prompt already contains the full sense protocol (it IS the sense_loop.md template, self-contained). The think/research/exporter are subagent prompts referenced by path. These are \"执行期按需\" subagent prompts. I'll leave as-is, OR inline the sense/think/research/exporter SKILLS. Hmm.\n\nActually, for BuildHumanLoop, the \"主产物\" is the sense_loop prompt (mainFile). It already IS self-contained (contains the full SENSE protocol). The subagent prompts (think/research/exporter) are separate files by design (they're registered as pi agents via env). So BuildHumanLoop is already \"单文件内聚\" in the sense that the main prompt is self-contained. I'll leave it.\n\nOK let me also double check: does the `go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/...` currently pass? Let me run it first to establish a baseline (before making changes). This is the RED phase — I should verify current state.\n\nActually, the task says to follow TDD: RED first (write failing test), then GREEN. The task10.py test is the acceptance test. But I should also add Go unit tests for `ReadEmbeddedSkill` and the builder inlining.\n\nLet me first establish baseline: run go build + go test.\n\nLet me also check: is there a `doing_check` still referenced anywhere that I need to worry about? The task prompt says to run `rick tools doing_check job_35`, but that command no longer exists (task8 removed it). The actual gate is `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py .rick/jobs/job_35/doing`. I'll use that.\n\nLet me establish the baseline now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_UfM4OLI9wXWWnza9nGZx7404","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && go build ./... 2>&1 | head -40 && echo \"BUILD_EXIT=$?\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_UcpRoRlhlHSmfziIgGwg1050","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/... 2>&1 | tail